window.SEAFLOOR_EN={"海底物理世界":"Seafloor Physics World","海底三维场景，可拖动旋转视角，滚轮或双指缩放；也可用方向键转动、+/− 缩放；按 G 键用文字描述当前画面":"3D undersea scene: drag to look around, scroll or pinch to zoom; or use the arrow keys to turn and +/− to zoom; press G for a text description of the view","透光层 · 上层带":"Sunlight zone · epipelagic","水温 28 °C":"Water 28 °C","南海西沙群岛珊瑚礁":"Paracel Islands coral reef, South China Sea","下潜深度剖面，珠穆朗玛峰按比例放在海沟中":"Dive depth profile, with Mount Everest drawn to scale inside the trench","关闭":"Close","展览模式：自动导览整片海洋":"Exhibition mode: an automatic tour of the whole ocean","展览模式":"Exhibition mode","上一站":"Previous stop","语音讲解：开":"Narration: on","暂停":"Pause","下一站":"Next stop","退出（Esc）":"Exit (Esc)","镜头会自动环绕，你也可以随时拖动画面。每站约 20 秒，配有语音讲解（可关闭），最后一站一路下潜到海沟底。":"The camera circles on its own, and you can drag the view at any time. Each stop lasts about 20 seconds with spoken narration (can be turned off); the last stop dives all the way to the bottom of the trench.","把当前画面做成明信片":"Turn the current view into a postcard","拍明信片":"Take a postcard","自由驾驶":"Free piloting","退出驾驶（Esc）":"Stop piloting (Esc)","W/S 前进后退 · A/D 左右平移 · Q/E 下潜上浮 · ←/→ 转向 · 拖动画面转头 · 点击生物仍可识别":"W/S forward/back · A/D strafe · Q/E dive/rise · ←/→ turn · drag to look around · you can still click animals to identify them","左下摇杆移动 · 右侧按钮上浮/下潜 · 拖动画面转头":"Joystick (bottom left) to move · buttons on the right to rise/dive · drag to look around","上浮":"Rise","下潜":"Dive","开始下潜":"Start dive","自动倍速":"Auto speed","×1 真实":"×1 real time","声音：关":"Sound: off","下潜深度":"Dive depth","拖动进度条可直接跳到任意深度；“自动倍速”在生物多的浅处放慢、在空旷的深处加快。":"Drag the progress bar to jump to any depth. “Auto speed” slows down in the busy shallows and speeds up in the empty deep.","控制台":"Console","用文字描述当前画面（G 键）":"Describe the current view in text (G key)","文字描述":"Describe","玩法说明":"How to use","收起":"Hide","这里的每个场景都按真实地点和实测数据搭建：光在水里怎样衰减、波浪和海流怎样推动海藻与水母、哪种生物会出现在哪个深度和水温。拖动画面转动视角，滚轮或双指缩放，点击生物可以看它是谁。":"Every scene here is built from a real place and measured data: how light fades in water, how waves and currents move seaweed and jellyfish, which animals live at which depth and temperature. Drag to turn the view, scroll or pinch to zoom, and click an animal to see what it is.","真实地点":"Real places","下潜：关岛礁壁 → 马里亚纳海沟 10,935 m":"Dive: Guam reef wall → Mariana Trench 10,935 m","重走 2012：卡梅隆独自下潜挑战者深渊":"Relive 2012: James Cameron’s solo dive to the Challenger Deep","北太平洋开阔大洋 · 昼夜垂直迁移（24 小时快进）":"Open North Pacific · daily vertical migration (24 h fast-forward)","下潜：三沙永乐龙洞 · 蓝洞 301 m":"Dive: Yongle Blue Hole, Sansha · 301 m","西沙 · 珊瑚礁":"Paracels · coral reef","三亚 · 珊瑚产卵之夜":"Sanya · coral spawning night","陵水 · 海草床与红树林":"Lingshui · seagrass and mangroves","南麂列岛 · 岩礁潮间带":"Nanji Islands · rocky intertidal","南极 · 海冰之下":"Antarctica · under the sea ice","北极 · 浮冰边缘":"Arctic · floe edge","蒙特雷 · 巨藻林":"Monterey · kelp forest","特鲁克 · 沉船鱼礁":"Truk · wreck reef","红海 · 中光层礁":"Red Sea · mesophotic reef","挪威 · 冷水珊瑚礁 320 m":"Norway · cold-water coral reef 320 m","南海陆坡 600 m":"South China Sea slope 600 m","海马冷泉 1390 m":"Haima cold seep 1390 m","蒙特雷峡谷 · 鲸落 1800 m":"Monterey Canyon · whale fall 1800 m","墨西哥湾 · 海底盐池 650 m":"Gulf of Mexico · brine pool 650 m","西南印度洋 · 龙旂热液区 2800 m":"SW Indian Ocean · Longqi vent field 2800 m","加州 · 海山章鱼花园 3200 m":"California · seamount octopus garden 3200 m","太平洋 · 深海平原 4100 m":"Pacific · abyssal plain 4100 m","珊瑚产卵之夜":"Coral spawning night","当地时间":"Local time","潮汐：海水的涨落":"Tides: the rise and fall of the sea","潮位":"Tide level","❚❚ 暂停潮汐":"❚❚ Pause tide","半日潮：约 12 小时 25 分涨落一次。这里把潮差简化为 4 m，播放速度是 1 秒相当于 15 分钟。海面以上的部分不显示，就像潜水时只能看到水下的那一半。":"Semidiurnal tide: one rise and fall about every 12 h 25 min. The tidal range is simplified to 4 m, and playback runs at 15 minutes per second. Anything above the sea surface is not shown, just as a diver only sees the underwater half.","鲸落：沉到海底之后":"Whale fall: after sinking to the seafloor","经过的时间":"Time elapsed","3 个月":"3 months","昼夜垂直迁移 · 回声测深图":"Daily vertical migration · echogram","24 小时回声测深图：横轴是一天中的时间，纵轴是 0 到 1000 米深度，暖色是动物密集的声散射层。点击可跳到对应的时间和深度。":"24-hour echogram: the horizontal axis is the time of day, the vertical axis is depth from 0 to 1000 m, and warm colours are the sound-scattering layers of dense animals. Click to jump to that time and depth.","模拟船上 38 kHz 测深仪看到的画面：暖色是动物密集的“声散射层”，主要来自灯笼鱼的鳔。顶部色条是太阳高度，白线是现在，虚线是你所在的深度。点击图上任意位置，可以跳到那个时间和深度。":"What a ship’s 38 kHz echo sounder would show: warm colours are the “sound-scattering layers” of dense animals, mostly from lanternfish swim bladders. The bar at the top is the sun’s height, the white line is now, and the dashed line is your depth. Click anywhere on the chart to jump to that time and depth.","你所在的深度":"Your depth","时间与照明":"Time and lighting","白天":"Day","夜潜":"Night dive","手电关":"Torch off","白光手电":"White torch","蓝光手电":"Blue torch","白光手电照亮约十来米。蓝光手电配黄色滤镜（荧光潜水的标准做法）：滤掉反射的蓝光，只剩珊瑚、海葵自己发出的荧光，夜里最明显。在黑暗里（夜潜或 200 m 以下）用手指或鼠标快速划过画面，能看到浮游生物被惊扰发出的蓝光。拖动画面可转动视角，镜头空闲时会自动缓慢环绕。":"The white torch lights about ten metres. The blue torch is used with a yellow filter (the standard fluorescence-diving method): the filter blocks reflected blue light so only the fluorescence of corals and anemones remains, clearest at night. In the dark (at night or below 200 m), swipe a finger or the mouse quickly across the view to see plankton flash blue when disturbed. Drag to turn the view; when idle the camera slowly circles on its own.","高画质":"High quality","流畅（手机）":"Smooth (phones)","流畅模式降低渲染分辨率、关闭泛光，并把海草、藤壶、章鱼等大量重复的生物减到约一半。打开页面后如果明显卡顿，会自动切换到流畅模式。":"Smooth mode lowers the render resolution, turns off bloom and cuts large numbers of repeated life such as seagrass, barnacles and octopuses to about half. If the page is clearly stuttering after it opens, it switches to smooth mode automatically.","自动漫游镜头":"Auto-roaming camera","声音（合成模拟：浪声、呼吸与气泡、抹香鲸的咔嗒声、深海低鸣）":"Sound (synthesised: surf, breathing and bubbles, sperm whale clicks, deep-sea rumble)","图鉴":"Field guide","点击画面中的生物，可以看它是谁。遇见过的生物才会显示名字。科学家估计海洋物种总数约 220 万，其中九成左右还没有被描述过。":"Click an animal in the scene to see what it is. Only animals you have met show their names. Scientists estimate there are about 2.2 million marine species, around 90% of them not yet described.","共享图鉴":"Shared field guide","打开这个页面的人共用一本图鉴。每个名字后面的小数字，是有多少位探险者遇见过它；数字越小越稀罕。没遇见过的生物也会显示人数，可以当作线索。":"Everyone who opens this page shares one field guide. The small number after each name is how many explorers have met it; the smaller the number, the rarer it is. Animals you have not met still show their count, which you can use as a clue.","探险任务":"Expeditions","每个任务都有进度；没完成的任务旁有“前往”按钮，点一下直接去对应地点。完成时会显示一条科学事实。进度只保存在这台设备的浏览器里。":"Each expedition shows its progress; unfinished ones have a “Go” button that takes you straight to the right place. A science fact appears when you complete one. Progress is saved only in this browser on this device.","地图与物理实验":"Map and physics experiments","海底地形总览：真实测深数据":"Seafloor relief: real bathymetry","把海水抽干后的地球，以及各个地点在哪里":"The Earth with the sea drained away, and where each place is","声音实验：深海声道（SOFAR）":"Sound experiment: the deep sound channel (SOFAR)","为什么鲸的叫声能传几千公里":"Why whale calls can travel thousands of kilometres","压力实验：把泡沫杯带到海底":"Pressure experiment: take a foam cup to the seafloor","同样是压力，气球、泡沫杯和一瓶水为什么结果完全不同":"Same pressure, so why do a balloon, a foam cup and a bottle of water end up so different?","VR 模式":"VR mode","手机分屏 VR":"Phone split-screen VR","画面分成左右两半，分别给左眼和右眼看。把手机横放进纸盒 VR 眼镜（Cardboard 一类）就有立体感":"The view is split into left and right halves, one for each eye. Turn the phone sideways and put it in a cardboard VR viewer to see in 3D","进入头显 VR":"Enter headset VR","在 Quest 等 VR 头显的浏览器里可用：转头看四周，左摇杆朝视线方向游动，右摇杆转身和升降":"Works in the browser of headsets such as Quest: turn your head to look around, left stick swims where you look, right stick turns and moves up and down","成年人两眼平均相距约 6.3 cm，两只眼看到的画面略有不同，大脑靠这点差别判断远近。VR 模式按 6.4 cm 的眼距分别渲染左右眼。当前地点、下潜和时间设置都会保留，在 VR 里也能一路潜到海沟底。":"Adult eyes are about 6.3 cm apart on average, so each eye sees a slightly different picture and the brain uses the difference to judge distance. VR mode renders each eye with a 6.4 cm separation. Your current place, dive and time settings are kept, and you can dive all the way to the trench in VR too.","此处可见":"What you can see here","此处剩余阳光（相对水面）":"Sunlight left here (relative to the surface)","红 650nm":"Red 650 nm","绿 550nm":"Green 550 nm","蓝 450nm":"Blue 450 nm","对数刻度（10⁻⁶ – 100%）。红光最先被水吸收，所以越深越蓝。":"Log scale (10⁻⁶ – 100%). Water absorbs red light first, so the deeper you go the bluer it gets.","环境参数（可自行调整）":"Environment (adjustable)","海底深度":"Seafloor depth","海水温度":"Water temperature","清澈大洋":"Clear ocean","一般大洋":"Typical ocean","温带近岸":"Temperate coast","近岸浑水":"Turbid coast","海流速度":"Current speed","海流去向（相对波向）":"Current direction (relative to waves)","有效波高":"Significant wave height","波周期":"Wave period","太阳高度角":"Sun elevation","模拟人眼适应（暗适应与色彩恒常；关闭则按相机看到的真实亮度和颜色显示）":"Simulate the human eye (dark adaptation and colour constancy; off shows the true brightness and colour a camera would record)","实时读数":"Live readings","漫衰减系数 K":"Diffuse attenuation K","1% 绿光深度":"Depth of 1% green light","水平能见度（约）":"Horizontal visibility (approx.)","水中太阳天顶角":"Sun zenith angle in water","波长":"Wavelength","海底波浪流速":"Wave-driven flow at the seafloor","离底 1 m 海流":"Current 1 m above the bottom","沙纹":"Sand ripples","海水黏度":"Seawater viscosity","2 mm 气泡上升速度":"Rise speed of a 2 mm bubble","气泡升到水面后":"When the bubble reaches the surface","场景用到的物理与生态规则":"Physical and ecological rules used in the scenes","光谱衰减":"Spectral attenuation","：Beer–Lambert":": Beer–Lambert","，红、绿、蓝分别计算；K":", computed separately for red, green and blue; K","由吸收 a、散射 b 按 Kirk 公式":"comes from absorption a and scattering b by Kirk’s formula","得出。":".","水色与视距":"Water colour and visibility","：视线按":": the line of sight fades as","衰减，背景水色来自散射比 b/(a+b)。":", and the background colour comes from the scattering ratio b/(a+b).","光柱（丁达尔效应）":"Light shafts (Tyndall effect)","：阳光被水中颗粒散射才看得见，亮度随散射系数 b 增大，随深度按 K":": sunlight is visible only because particles in the water scatter it; brightness rises with the scattering coefficient b and fades with depth as K","衰减。":".","斯涅尔窗":"Snell’s window","：抬头看水面，只有 97.2° 圆锥内能看到天空（临界角 48.6°）。":": looking up at the surface, you see the sky only inside a 97.2° cone (critical angle 48.6°).","波浪与海流":"Waves and currents","：线性波理论":": linear wave theory","的往复流，叠加海底对数边界层海流":"gives the oscillating flow, added to a logarithmic bottom boundary-layer current","；海带、水母、海葵触手、颗粒都随之运动。水母本身是浮游生物，主要随水漂。":"; kelp, jellyfish, anemone tentacles and particles all move with it. Jellyfish are plankton and mostly drift with the water.","海底地形总览":"Seafloor relief overview","：使用 NOAA 的 ETOPO 20 角分全球地形数据（每格约 37 km），压缩为 8 位（约 60 m 一档），配合西北方向光照做晕渲。剖面沿两点间的经纬度直线取样，竖直方向放大显示。格点较粗，窄海沟会显示得偏浅。":": uses NOAA’s ETOPO 20-arc-minute global relief data (each cell about 37 km), packed into 8 bits (about 60 m per step), with hill shading lit from the north-west. Profiles are sampled along a straight latitude–longitude line between two points, with vertical exaggeration. The grid is coarse, so narrow trenches look shallower than they are.","压力实验":"Pressure experiment","：压强":": pressure","。气球按玻意耳定律":". The balloon follows Boyle’s law","；水的压缩系数取约 4.6×10⁻¹⁰ /Pa；泡沫杯用简化模型：含 95% 空气、约 6 个大气压后气泡壁开始被压垮，之后按玻意耳定律压缩并且不再恢复。泡沫杯的这两个参数是假设，不是测量值，真实杯子会有差异。":"; water compressibility is about 4.6×10⁻¹⁰ /Pa; the foam cup uses a simplified model: 95% air, cell walls start to collapse at about 6 atmospheres, after which it compresses by Boyle’s law and never recovers. These two foam parameters are assumptions, not measurements, and real cups differ.","深海声道":"Deep sound channel","：声速用 Mackenzie（1981）公式，由下潜路线的水温剖面、盐度 34.6 和深度算出；声线按斯涅尔定律":": sound speed from the Mackenzie (1981) formula, using the dive route’s temperature profile, salinity 34.6 and depth; rays are traced by Snell’s law","cosθ/c=常数":"cosθ/c = constant","追踪，向声速慢的一侧弯折。声道轴大约在 1 km 深处，不碰海面也不碰海底的声线才算“被困住”。1,000 km 外的到达时间用同样的声线计算，播放时用短促的音调代表每条声线的到达。":"and bend towards the slower side. The channel axis is about 1 km deep; only rays that touch neither the surface nor the bottom count as “trapped”. Arrival times 1,000 km away use the same rays, and playback marks each ray’s arrival with a short tone.","触碰发光":"Touch glow","：甲藻等浮游生物在水流剪切力超过约 0.1–0.3 Pa 时闪光（Latz 等的实验）。在黑暗的水里用手指或鼠标划过，按手掌大小（约 0.1 m）的物体计算边界层剪切力":": dinoflagellates and other plankton flash when the shear stress of the flow exceeds about 0.1–0.3 Pa (experiments by Latz et al.). Swipe a finger or the mouse through dark water: the boundary-layer shear is computed for a hand-sized object (about 0.1 m)","，速度超过约 0.3 m/s 才会亮，越快越多；自由驾驶时潜水器本身也会激起闪光。每次闪光持续零点几秒。点击冠水母会触发它的“防盗警报”光环，点击深海的竹珊瑚会让一圈光沿枝条传开。白天的浅水太亮，看不到这些光。":", so it lights up only above about 0.3 m/s, and more the faster you go; when piloting, the vehicle itself also sets off flashes. Each flash lasts a fraction of a second. Clicking an Atolla jellyfish triggers its “burglar alarm” ring of light, and clicking a deep bamboo coral sends a wave of light along its branches. Shallow water by day is too bright to see any of this.","：推进器加速度约 0.9 m/s²，水的阻力与速度平方成正比，最高速度约 1 m/s，和小型水下机器人或游泳的潜水员相当。你在水里还会随海流（海底附近按对数边界层减弱）和波浪的往复流一起漂动，所以在浅礁上会被涌浪推来推去。60 m 的缆绳是按系缆式水下机器人设定的。":": thruster acceleration about 0.9 m/s², water drag proportional to speed squared, top speed about 1 m/s, similar to a small underwater robot or a swimming diver. You also drift with the current (weaker near the bottom, following the log boundary layer) and the oscillating wave flow, so on a shallow reef the swell pushes you around. The 60 m tether matches a tethered underwater robot.","沉船鱼礁":"Wreck reef","：参照特鲁克泻湖的富士川丸（长 133 m、宽 17.8 m，直立于约 34 m 深的沙底，后桅伸出水面，前吊杆柱顶距水面约 3 m）。软珊瑚沿桅杆、吊杆生长，甲板上有小块硬珊瑚，船体表面按海绵、海鞘、锈蚀的斑块着色；船体轮廓与舱口位置是按照片和潜水描述简化的。":": modelled on the Fujikawa Maru in Truk Lagoon (133 m long, 17.8 m wide, sitting upright on sand about 34 m deep, the aft mast reaching the surface and the top of the forward kingpost about 3 m below it). Soft corals grow along the masts and booms, small hard corals sit on the deck, and the hull is coloured in patches of sponge, sea squirt and rust; the hull outline and hatch positions are simplified from photos and divers’ descriptions.","冷水珊瑚礁":"Cold-water coral reef","：参照挪威罗弗敦外海的勒斯特礁（约 35–43 km 长，2002 年发现）。造礁的深水石珊瑚（Desmophyllum pertusum，旧称 Lophelia pertusa）没有共生藻，生活在约 4–12 °C 的海水里；挪威 180–304 m 处的实测年线性生长只有约 1.3–2.4 mm。珊瑚灌丛底部画成死骨架、顶端为活体，白色与橙色两种颜色型约七三开；这一比例和礁上的生物组合是示意，不是实测。":": modelled on the Røst Reef off Lofoten, Norway (about 35–43 km long, discovered in 2002). The reef-building deep-water stony coral (Desmophyllum pertusum, formerly Lophelia pertusa) has no symbiotic algae and lives in water of about 4–12 °C; its measured linear growth at 180–304 m in Norway is only about 1.3–2.4 mm a year. The coral thickets are drawn with dead skeleton below and living tips above, in white and orange colour forms about 70:30; this ratio and the reef’s community are illustrative, not measured.","海冰之下":"Under the sea ice","：参照南极麦克默多湾的冰下潜水记录：海冰约 2 m（6–8 英尺）厚，水温约 −1.9 °C，冬末春初海水几乎没有浮游生物，非常清澈。冰下的环境光按海冰和积雪只透过约 3.5% 计算，积雪薄的地方更亮；冰洞里的光柱则是完整的日光。冰底的冰藻、片状冰、冰鱼和其他动物按文献描述的外观建模。":": based on under-ice diving records from McMurdo Sound, Antarctica: sea ice about 2 m (6–8 ft) thick, water about −1.9 °C, and at the end of winter almost no plankton, so the water is very clear. Ambient light under the ice assumes the ice and snow let through about 3.5%, more where the snow is thin; the light shaft in the dive hole is full daylight. The ice algae, platelet ice, icefish and other animals are modelled on their descriptions in the literature.","珊瑚产卵":"Coral spawning","：参照海南三亚鹿回头岸礁 2009–2021 年的观察：22 种珊瑚中鹿角珊瑚占 14 种，主要在农历三月产卵，约 21 点后开始、持续约一小时，卵精束多为红色。上浮速度按浮力与黏滞阻力估算：取直径约 1.5 mm、比海水轻约 1% 的卵精束，约每秒 1 cm；到水面后约一小时散开。具体在哪一夜产卵年年不同，无法精确预测。":": based on observations at the Luhuitou fringing reef, Sanya, Hainan, 2009–2021: 14 of the 22 coral species are Acropora, which spawn mainly in the third lunar month, starting after about 9 pm and lasting about an hour, with mostly red egg–sperm bundles. Their rise speed is estimated from buoyancy and viscous drag: bundles about 1.5 mm across and about 1% lighter than seawater rise about 1 cm per second, then spread out about an hour after reaching the surface. The exact night varies from year to year and cannot be predicted precisely.","蓝洞":"Blue hole","：参照三沙永乐龙洞（深约 301 m，洞口约 130 m 宽、洞底约 32 m）。洞里的水几乎与外海隔绝，分成含氧层（0–70 m）、化学跃层（70–100 m）和含硫化氢的无氧层（100 m 以下）；水温由表层约 30 °C 降到洞底约 15 °C。浑浊层按硫氧化细菌（100–140 m）和颗粒有机碳峰值（约 150 m）的位置设定，在那里把散射系数调高约 16 倍，所以手电光会化成一片雾。浑浊层的具体浊度是推算，不是实测值。":": based on the Yongle Blue Hole, Sansha (about 301 m deep, mouth about 130 m wide, bottom about 32 m across). Its water is almost cut off from the open sea and is layered into an oxygenated layer (0–70 m), a chemocline (70–100 m) and an anoxic layer with hydrogen sulfide (below 100 m); temperature falls from about 30 °C at the surface to about 15 °C at the bottom. The turbid layers are set where sulfur-oxidising bacteria (100–140 m) and the peak of particulate organic carbon (about 150 m) are found, with scattering raised about 16-fold, so a torch beam turns into fog. The exact turbidity is an estimate, not a measurement.","海底盐池":"Brine pool","：参照墨西哥湾 NR1 盐池（约 650 m）。卤水含盐量约为海水的 4 倍，密度约 1.09 g/cm³（海水约 1.027），积在一个漏斗形洼地里，大部分不到 2 m 深，冒甲烷气泡的地方深得多。湖面的波是两种液体之间的“内波”，回复力是约化重力":": based on the NR1 brine pool in the Gulf of Mexico (about 650 m). The brine is about 4 times as salty as seawater, with a density of about 1.09 g/cm³ (seawater about 1.027), pooled in a funnel-shaped hollow mostly less than 2 m deep, much deeper where methane bubbles out. Waves on the lake are “internal waves” between two liquids, with reduced gravity","，按深水色散":"as the restoring force, travelling by the deep-water dispersion relation","传播，所以又慢又软。反射按菲涅耳公式计算，两种水的折射率只差约 1%，只有贴近湖面斜看时才像镜子。":", so they are slow and soft. Reflection follows Fresnel’s equations; the two waters differ in refractive index by only about 1%, so the surface looks like a mirror only when seen at a grazing angle.","昼夜垂直迁移":"Daily vertical migration","：海面光照由太阳高度算出（日落时约为正午的 0.4%，民用晨昏蒙影结束时约 0.003%，再暗到星光）。每类动物都追随自己偏好的那一档亮度（“等光面”）：":": surface light is computed from the sun’s height (about 0.4% of noon at sunset, about 0.003% at the end of civil twilight, then down to starlight). Each group of animals follows its own preferred light level (an “isolume”):","z=z_白天+ln(E/E_正午)/K_d(蓝)":"z = z_day + ln(E/E_noon)/K_d(blue)","，在白天深度和夜间深度之间，再受游速限制（灯笼鱼约 8 m/min，磷虾约 3 m/min）。白天灯笼鱼层在约 450 m，正是二战声呐发现的“假海底”的深度；银斧鱼几乎不迁移，作为对照。月光、云和季节的影响没有模拟。":", between its day and night depths, limited by swimming speed (lanternfish about 8 m/min, krill about 3 m/min). By day the lanternfish layer sits at about 450 m, the depth of the “false bottom” found by wartime sonar; hatchetfish barely migrate and serve as a comparison. Moonlight, clouds and seasons are not simulated.","热液喷口":"Hydrothermal vents","：参照西南印度洋中脊的龙旂热液区（约 2,800 m，Copley 等 2016 年的调查）。黑烟由超过 300 °C 的热液遇冷析出的金属硫化物构成；羽流按浮力羽流理论计算，半径约为上升高度的 0.12 倍，上升速度随高度按 z":": based on the Longqi vent field on the Southwest Indian Ridge (about 2,800 m, surveyed by Copley et al. in 2016). Black smoke is metal sulfides precipitating as fluid above 300 °C meets cold water; the plume follows buoyant-plume theory, with a radius about 0.12 times its rise height and a rise speed slowing with height as z","减慢，并被海流吹弯。动物按离热液的远近分带：最内圈是盲虾、雪人蟹和铁甲蜗牛，往外是巨螺和贻贝，最外圈是柄藤壶和海葵。":"and bent by the current. Animals are zoned by distance from the vent fluid: blind shrimp, yeti crabs and scaly-foot snails innermost, then giant snails and mussels, with stalked barnacles and anemones outermost.","鲸落":"Whale fall","：参照 MBARI 在加州蒙特雷峡谷对灰鲸鲸落的长期观测。演替分三段并有重叠：食腐动物（盲鳗、睡鲨，约 2 年内吃光鲸肉，每天 40–60 kg）、机会主义者（约 2 年，食骨蠕虫等）、化能合成阶段（细菌分解骨中油脂放出硫化氢，贻贝和细菌席，可持续约 50 年甚至更久）。食骨蠕虫 2002 年在这条峡谷 2,893 m 的灰鲸骨头上首次被发现。":": based on MBARI’s long-term observations of grey whale falls in Monterey Canyon, California. The succession has three overlapping stages: scavengers (hagfish and sleeper sharks strip the flesh within about 2 years, 40–60 kg a day), opportunists (about 2 years, bone-eating worms and others), and a chemosynthetic stage (bacteria break down the oil in the bones and release hydrogen sulfide, feeding mussels and bacterial mats for about 50 years or longer). Bone-eating Osedax worms were first discovered in 2002 on grey whale bones at 2,893 m in this canyon.","岩壁":"Rock wall","：下潜从关岛的礁壁开始（关岛的礁坡在约 20 m 处开始陡降，壁上长着软珊瑚、海扇、海鞭和管状海绵），随后离开岩壁进入开阔大洋；6,000 m 以下贴近海沟内壁；接近底部时进入海沟轴部平坦的沉积盆地。挑战者深渊实际位于关岛西南约 330 km，这是一条把真实地形串起来的路线。":": the dive starts at a reef wall on Guam (Guam’s reef slope drops steeply from about 20 m, with soft corals, sea fans, sea whips and tube sponges on the wall), then leaves the wall for the open ocean; below 6,000 m it follows the inner wall of the trench, and near the bottom it enters the flat sediment basin along the trench axis. The Challenger Deep actually lies about 330 km south-west of Guam; this is a route that strings real terrain together.","重走 2012":"Relive 2012","：按卡梅隆真实下潜的时间线：05:15 出发，下潜 2 小时 36 分，在海底停留三个多小时，上浮 70 分钟；当时没有岩壁可贴，海底“完全没有起伏”，画面据此呈现。":": follows the real timeline of Cameron’s dive: departure at 05:15, a 2 h 36 min descent, more than three hours on the bottom and a 70-minute ascent. There was no wall to follow, and he described the seafloor as “completely flat”, which is how it is shown.","潜水器灯":"Sub lights","：下潜模式里 250 m 以下会自动打开潜水器的照明灯，比手电强得多，但在海水里也只能照亮十来米。":": in dive mode the submersible’s lights switch on automatically below 250 m. They are far stronger than a torch, but in seawater still light only about ten metres.","手电":"Torch","：光要走“去”和“回”两段水路，按 e^(−c·2d) 衰减。夜里光束中的悬浮颗粒会反光，这是潜水员熟悉的“背散射”。":": light travels the water path twice, there and back, so it fades as e^(−c·2d). At night, particles in the beam reflect light: the “backscatter” divers know well.","生物荧光":"Biofluorescence","：珊瑚和海葵的荧光蛋白吸收蓝光、发出绿光或橙红光，所以蓝光手电下最亮。":": fluorescent proteins in corals and anemones absorb blue light and give off green or orange-red light, so they glow brightest under a blue torch.","生物发光":"Bioluminescence","：夜光藻被水流扰动会闪蓝光（鱼游过留下光迹）；灯笼鱼的发光器、鮟鱇的诱饵、冠水母的“报警”光环、竹珊瑚沿枝条传播的光波，都是 470 nm 左右的蓝光，正是海水最透明的颜色。":": the dinoflagellate Noctiluca flashes blue when disturbed (fish leave trails of light); the photophores of lanternfish, the lure of the anglerfish, the “alarm” ring of Atolla and the waves of light along bamboo corals are all blue light around 470 nm, exactly the colour seawater transmits best.","人眼适应":"Eye adaptation","：暗适应调节整体亮度；色彩恒常让大脑部分补偿海水造成的偏色，所以潜水员看到的颜色比相机直接拍到的更丰富。关闭后显示相机看到的样子。":": dark adaptation sets the overall brightness; colour constancy lets the brain partly correct the colour cast of the water, so divers see richer colour than a camera records. Turn it off to see what a camera would see.","栉水母的彩虹":"The comb jelly’s rainbow","：不是发光，是栉板纤毛把入射光衍射成彩色，所以没有光照时就看不到彩虹。":": it is not light the animal makes. Its comb-plate cilia diffract incoming light into colours, so with no light there is no rainbow.","生物分布":"Where animals live","：巨藻 ≤20 °C；造礁珊瑚 ≥18 °C 且光照 ≥1%（光越弱越长成盘状）；海葵与小丑鱼、砗磲需要温暖明亮的浅水；柳珊瑚扇面垂直于海流；灯笼鱼白天在 200–1200 m；鮟鱇 ≥700 m；冠水母 ≥400 m；冷泉有贻贝床、管栖蠕虫和白色细菌席。":": giant kelp ≤20 °C; reef-building corals ≥18 °C and ≥1% light (growing into plates where light is weaker); anemones with clownfish, and giant clams, need warm, bright shallow water; sea fan faces stand across the current; lanternfish spend the day at 200–1200 m; anglerfish ≥700 m; Atolla ≥400 m; cold seeps have mussel beds, tubeworms and white bacterial mats.","气泡":"Bubbles","：玻意耳定律":": Boyle’s law","上升中膨胀；浅水的气泡是潜水员（你）呼出的，每 4–5 秒一次；冷泉的气泡是海底渗出的甲烷。显示尺寸放大了 3 倍。":"makes them grow as they rise; in shallow water the bubbles are the diver’s (your) breath, every 4–5 seconds; at cold seeps they are methane seeping from the seafloor. They are drawn 3 times larger than life.","鱼群":"Fish schools","：Boids 群游规则；沙丁鱼会绕圈形成“鱼饵球”；鱼会顶着海流游；体色背深腹浅（反荫蔽）。":": Boids flocking rules; sardines circle into “bait balls”; fish swim into the current; bodies are dark above and pale below (countershading).","压强":"Pressure","：":": ","，ρ=1025 kg/m³。挑战者深渊底部约 1,100 个大气压。":", ρ = 1025 kg/m³. At the bottom of the Challenger Deep it is about 1,100 atmospheres.","水温剖面":"Temperature profile","：下潜模式按西太平洋典型剖面：表层约 28 °C，温跃层在 100–400 m 迅速降温，1,000 m 约 4.5 °C，4,000 m 约 1.5 °C；海沟底部因海水被压缩升温（绝热增温），又回升到约 2.5 °C。":": dive mode uses a typical western Pacific profile: about 28 °C at the surface, falling quickly through the thermocline at 100–400 m, about 4.5 °C at 1,000 m and about 1.5 °C at 4,000 m; at the bottom of the trench the water warms again to about 2.5 °C because it is compressed (adiabatic heating).","下潜速度":"Descent speed","：深潜器真实下潜速度约 1 m/s，到挑战者深渊要 3 个小时左右（1960 年的里雅斯特号用了 4 小时 47 分）。":": deep submersibles really descend at about 1 m/s, so reaching the Challenger Deep takes about 3 hours (the Trieste took 4 h 47 min in 1960).","鲸和鱼的尾巴":"Whale and fish tails","：鲸的尾鳍是水平的，上下摆动；鱼和鲨鱼的尾鳍是竖直的，左右摆动。":": a whale’s flukes are horizontal and beat up and down; the tail fins of fish and sharks are vertical and sweep side to side.","气泡的声音":"The sound of bubbles","：每个气泡会以 Minnaert 共振频率":": each bubble rings at its Minnaert resonance frequency","发声，大气泡低沉，小气泡清脆；越深压强越大，音调越高。":"; large bubbles sound low and small ones bright, and the deeper they are, the higher the pressure and the pitch.","深度分布":"Depth ranges","：狮子鱼最深约 8,200 m，再深体内用来对抗压强的渗透调节分子（TMAO）就不够用了；大王乌贼在 300–1,000 m，至今只被拍到过寥寥几次。":": snailfish live down to about 8,200 m; deeper than that, the osmolyte (TMAO) their bodies use to resist pressure runs out. Giant squid live at 300–1,000 m and have been filmed only a handful of times.","更新记录、路线图与资料来源":"Update log, roadmap and sources","研究思路、技术架构、遗留问题、可扩展方向和可搜索的资料库，整理在单独的":"Our research approach, technical architecture, open issues, ideas for extension and a searchable library of sources are collected on a separate","项目总览":"project overview","页面。":"page. (The development log below is in Chinese.)","海面附近水暖，声音跑得快；深处压强大，声音也跑得快；两者之间约 1 km 深处，声速最慢。声音总是往声速慢的一边弯，所以从这一层发出的声音会被上下来回“折”回来，像困在一条看不见的管道里，能传几千公里。":"Near the surface the water is warm and sound travels fast; in the deep the pressure is high and sound also travels fast; in between, at about 1 km, sound is slowest. Sound always bends towards the slower side, so sound from this layer is bent back again and again from above and below, as if trapped in an invisible pipe, and can travel thousands of kilometres.","左边是声速随深度的变化曲线，右边是从声源发出的 25 条声线在 300 km 范围内的路径":"Left: how sound speed changes with depth. Right: the paths of 25 rays from the source over 300 km","声源深度":"Source depth","听 1,000 km 外收到的声音":"Hear the sound received 1,000 km away","怎么看这张图：左边是声速随深度变化的曲线（按下潜路线的实测型水温剖面，用 Mackenzie 公式算出）；右边是从红点发出、上下各 12° 范围内的 25 条声线。试着把声源拖到海面附近或 4,000 m 深处，看还有多少声线能留在声道里。为了看清，图里的水平距离被压缩了：300 km 对 5 km 深。":"How to read the chart: on the left is sound speed against depth (computed with the Mackenzie formula from the measured-type temperature profile of the dive route); on the right are 25 rays from the red dot, spread 12° up and down. Try dragging the source near the surface or down to 4,000 m and see how many rays stay in the channel. To make it readable, horizontal distance is compressed: 300 km against 5 km of depth.","每往下 10 m，水压就增加约 1 个大气压。科考船上的传统是把画好图案的泡沫塑料杯挂在潜水器外面带下去，回来时它已经缩成了小杯子。这里把它和一个装空气的气球、一瓶水放在一起比较。":"Every 10 m down, water pressure rises by about one atmosphere. A tradition on research ships is to hang decorated foam cups outside the submersible; they come back shrunk into tiny cups. Here a cup is compared with an air-filled balloon and a bottle of water.","泡沫杯、气球和水瓶在当前深度下的大小，虚线是原来的大小":"The size of the foam cup, balloon and water bottle at the current depth; dashed lines show their original size","深度":"Depth","带到挑战者深渊":"Take them to the Challenger Deep","带回水面":"Bring them back to the surface","换一个新杯子":"New cup","为什么三者差别这么大：气球里全是空气，空气按玻意耳定律被压缩，体积和压强成反比，回到水面又弹回原样。泡沫塑料是约 95% 的空气关在无数小气泡里，压强大到一定程度，气泡壁被压垮、空气被挤掉，杯子均匀地缩小，而且再也回不去了，所以先下潜、再上浮，杯子还是小的。水几乎不能压缩，即使在 1 万多米深也只缩小约 5%；但正因为海水被压得稍微紧了一点，如果海水完全不能压缩，全球海平面会再高出约 30 m。":"Why the three end up so different: the balloon holds only air, which is compressed by Boyle’s law, its volume inversely proportional to pressure, and it springs back at the surface. Foam is about 95% air trapped in countless tiny cells; past a certain pressure the cell walls collapse and the air is squeezed out, so the cup shrinks evenly and never recovers. Go down and come back up, and the cup stays small. Water barely compresses, shrinking only about 5% even more than 10,000 m down; yet because seawater is squeezed slightly tighter, if it could not be compressed at all, global sea level would be about 30 m higher.","关于模型：泡沫杯的缩小是简化模型，假设泡沫含 95% 的空气、气泡壁在约 6 个大气压（约 50 m 深）后开始被压垮，之后按玻意耳定律压缩。真实的杯子会因泡沫的均匀程度、在深处停留的时间不同而缩得多一些或少一些，有的还会变形。":"About the model: the cup’s shrinking is a simplified model that assumes the foam is 95% air and its cell walls begin to collapse after about 6 atmospheres (about 50 m deep), then compress by Boyle’s law. Real cups shrink a bit more or less depending on how even the foam is and how long they stay deep, and some get distorted.","把海水抽干，地球是这个样子：大陆外缘是浅浅的陆架，往外是陡峭的陆坡和几千米深的大洋盆地；大洋中间横亘着连绵几万公里的洋中脊；太平洋边缘是一道道深深的海沟。红点是这个海底世界里的各个地点，点一下就能前往。":"Drain the oceans and this is the Earth: continents edged by shallow shelves, then steep slopes down to ocean basins thousands of metres deep; mid-ocean ridges running tens of thousands of kilometres through the oceans; and deep trenches lining the Pacific. Red dots are the places in this seafloor world; click one to go there.","全球海底与陆地地形图，红点是本页的各个地点":"Global relief map of the seafloor and land; red dots are the places in this page","把鼠标移到地图上，可以看到那里的经纬度和水深。":"Move the mouse over the map to see the latitude, longitude and depth there.","剖面：穿过马里亚纳海沟":"Profile: across the Mariana Trench","剖面：横穿大西洋中脊":"Profile: across the Mid-Atlantic Ridge","剖面：西南印度洋中脊（龙旂热液区附近）":"Profile: Southwest Indian Ridge (near the Longqi vent field)","剖面：南海":"Profile: South China Sea","所选两点之间的海底剖面":"Seafloor profile between the two chosen points","数据来源：美国国家海洋和大气管理局（NOAA）的 ETOPO 全球地形数据，分辨率 20 角分，每个格点约 37 km 宽，为了放进网页又压缩成约 60 m 一档。格点这么大，窄窄的海沟会被平均得变浅：这里马里亚纳海沟最深只显示约 9,000 m，实测是 10,935 m。所以这张图适合看“全球海底长什么样”，而页面里各个场景的近景地形仍是按资料描述生成的，不是逐米的实测地形。":"Data: ETOPO global relief data from the US National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) at 20-arc-minute resolution, each cell about 37 km wide, packed into steps of about 60 m to fit in a web page. With cells this large, narrow trenches are averaged shallower: the Mariana Trench shows only about 9,000 m here against a measured 10,935 m. So this map shows what the seafloor looks like worldwide, while the close-up terrain of each scene is generated from descriptions, not measured metre by metre.","海底明信片":"Seafloor postcard","刚才的画面，配上这里的地点、深度、水温和气压。":"The view you just saw, with the place, depth, water temperature and pressure.","当前画面做成的明信片":"A postcard made from the current view","保存图片":"Save image","此刻的画面":"The view right now","用文字说明你现在在哪里、周围的环境和附近看得见哪些生物（由近到远，括号里是相对你视线的方向和距离），方便使用读屏软件或看不清三维画面的人。随时按 G 键打开或关闭；关掉后可以用方向键转动视角、+/− 缩放，再按 G 看新的描述。":"A text account of where you are, the conditions around you and which animals you can see nearby (nearest first; in brackets, their direction from where you are looking and their distance), for screen-reader users and anyone who can’t see the 3D view well. Press G at any time to open or close it; after closing it, turn the view with the arrow keys and zoom with +/−, then press G again for a fresh description.","刷新":"Refresh","看什么":"What to look at","这是一个按真实地点和实测数据搭建的海底世界。光线、水色、波浪、海流、水温和压强都按物理公式计算，每种生物只会出现在它真实生活的深度、水温和环境里。控制台最下方的“场景用到的物理与生态规则”列出了所有依据。":"This is a seafloor world built from real places and measured data. Light, water colour, waves, currents, temperature and pressure are calculated from physical formulas, and each animal appears only at the depth, temperature and habitat where it really lives. “Physical and ecological rules used in the scenes” at the bottom of the console lists everything they are based on.","换地点、下潜":"Changing place and diving","在控制台“真实地点”里选一个地点，下面的介绍卡会告诉你那里是哪里、有什么看点。带边框的几项是“路线”：一路下潜到马里亚纳海沟、重走卡梅隆 2012 年的下潜、昼夜垂直迁移、三沙永乐龙洞。下潜时底部会出现进度条，可以暂停、调倍速，或拖动直接跳到任意深度。":"Pick a place under “Real places” in the console; the card below tells you where it is and what to look for. The items with a border are “routes”: a dive all the way to the Mariana Trench, a replay of Cameron’s 2012 dive, daily vertical migration, and the Yongle Blue Hole. While diving, a progress bar appears at the bottom: you can pause, change the speed, or drag to jump to any depth.","看和认":"Looking and identifying","拖动画面转动视角，滚轮或双指缩放（键盘：先点一下画面或按 Tab 选中它，方向键转动，+/− 缩放）；镜头空闲一会儿会自动缓慢环绕（可在“时间与照明”里关掉）。点击画面里的生物、烟囱、沉船等，会弹出说明卡。第一次遇见的生物会出现在“图鉴”里。":"Drag to turn the view, scroll or pinch to zoom (with a keyboard: click the view or Tab to it, then use the arrow keys to turn and +/− to zoom); when idle the camera slowly circles (you can turn this off under “Time and lighting”). Click animals, chimneys, wrecks and so on in the scene to open an information card. Animals you meet for the first time are added to the “Field guide”.","点左下角“自由驾驶”，自己开着水下机器人游。电脑：W/S 前进后退，A/D 左右平移，Q/E 下潜上浮，←/→ 转向，拖动画面转头，Esc 退出。手机：左下摇杆移动，右侧按钮上浮、下潜，拖动画面转头。最高约 1 m/s，海流和波浪会推着你漂，缆绳长 60 m。下潜路线中不能自由驾驶。":"Click “Free piloting” at the bottom left to drive an underwater robot yourself. Computer: W/S forward/back, A/D strafe, Q/E dive/rise, ←/→ turn, drag to look around, Esc to exit. Phone: joystick at the bottom left to move, buttons on the right to rise and dive, drag to look around. Top speed is about 1 m/s, currents and waves push you around, and the tether is 60 m long. Piloting is not available on dive routes.","文字描述（G 键）":"Text description (G key)","按 G 键或点控制台顶部的“文字描述”，会用文字列出你现在在哪里、水深、压强、水温、光线，以及附近看得见的生物和它们的一句介绍。适合使用读屏软件，或者看不清三维画面的时候。":"Press G, or “Describe” at the top of the console, for a text account of where you are, the depth, pressure, water temperature and light, and the animals you can see nearby with one line about each. Useful with a screen reader, or whenever the 3D view is hard to see.","“夜潜”切换昼夜。白光手电照亮约十来米；蓝光手电配黄色滤镜，用来看珊瑚、海葵的荧光。200 m 以下阳光几乎耗尽，需要手电或潜水器灯。":"“Night dive” switches between day and night. The white torch lights about ten metres; the blue torch is used with a yellow filter to see the fluorescence of corals and anemones. Below 200 m the sunlight is almost gone and you need a torch or the sub’s lights.","在黑暗的水里（夜潜，或 200 m 以下）用手指或鼠标在画面上快速划过，浮游生物会闪出蓝光，划得越快越亮；太慢不会亮，白天也看不到。在深海点击冠水母、竹珊瑚，会看到它们的发光反应。":"In dark water (a night dive, or below 200 m), swipe a finger or the mouse quickly across the view and plankton will flash blue: the faster you swipe, the brighter. Too slow and nothing lights up, and you cannot see it by day. In the deep, click an Atolla jellyfish or a bamboo coral to see their light displays.","探险任务与图鉴":"Expeditions and the field guide","“探险任务”给出 13 个探索目标，带进度和“前往”按钮，完成时会显示一条科学事实。任务进度只保存在这台设备的浏览器里。":"“Expeditions” gives you 13 goals to explore, with progress and a “Go” button; finishing one shows a science fact. Expedition progress is saved only in this browser on this device.","（在 Claude 里打开的版本才有共享图鉴；独立网站版本的图鉴只保存在这台设备上。）图鉴是所有打开这个页面的人共用的：名字后面的小数字表示多少位探险者遇见过这种生物。你遇见新生物后，几秒内会自动计入（只记录生物清单）。如果分享者给你的是“查看者”权限，你能看到数字，但自己的发现不会计入，只保存在本机；请分享者把你设为“参与者”即可。":"(Only the version opened in Claude has the shared field guide; on the standalone website the field guide is saved only on this device.) The field guide is shared by everyone who opens this page: the small number after a name is how many explorers have met that animal. When you meet a new animal it is counted within a few seconds (only the list of animals is recorded). If the person who shared the page gave you “viewer” access, you can see the numbers but your own finds are not counted and stay on your device; ask them to make you a “participant”.","特殊场景的控件":"Controls for special scenes","鲸落：拖动“经过的时间”看几十年的变化。昼夜垂直迁移：拖时间、拖深度，或点击回声测深图。珊瑚产卵之夜：拖动当地时间。蓝洞和海沟下潜：看左侧剖面图里你的位置。":"Whale fall: drag “Time elapsed” to watch decades of change. Daily vertical migration: drag the time or depth, or click the echogram. Coral spawning night: drag the local time. Blue hole and trench dives: see where you are on the profile at the left.","左下角“拍明信片”会把当前画面做成一张带地点、深度、水温和气压的图片，可以保存下来分享。":"“Take a postcard” at the bottom left turns the current view into a picture with the place, depth, water temperature and pressure, which you can save and share.","左下角“展览模式”（或欢迎页的“看 8 分钟展览导览”）会自动带你走过 16 个真实地点：珊瑚礁、海草床与红树林、岩礁潮间带、巨藻林、沉船、南极冰下、北极冰缘、珊瑚产卵、冷水珊瑚礁、冷泉、海底盐池、鲸落、热液喷口、海山章鱼花园、深海平原，最后一路下潜到马里亚纳海沟底。每站约 20 秒，配字幕和语音讲解（底部“语音讲解”按钮可以关掉）；镜头自动环绕，你也可以随时拖动。底部可以暂停、跳到上一站或下一站，按“退出”或 Esc 回到自由探索。":"“Exhibition mode” at the bottom left (or “Watch the 8-minute tour” on the welcome card) takes you through 16 real places automatically: coral reef, seagrass and mangroves, rocky intertidal, kelp forest, shipwreck, under the Antarctic ice, the Arctic floe edge, coral spawning, cold-water coral reef, cold seep, brine pool, whale fall, hydrothermal vents, the seamount octopus garden and the abyssal plain, finally diving all the way to the bottom of the Mariana Trench. Each stop lasts about 20 seconds with captions and spoken narration (the “Narration” button at the bottom turns it off); the camera circles automatically and you can drag at any time. At the bottom you can pause or skip to the previous or next stop; press “Exit” or Esc to go back to free exploring.","控制台“VR 模式”里点“手机分屏 VR”：把手机横过来，有纸盒 VR 眼镜就放进去。转动手机看四周（读不到陀螺仪时用手指拖动），轻点屏幕开始或停止游动，按“退出 VR”或 Esc 返回。用 VR 头显时，在头显自带的浏览器里打开本页，点“进入头显 VR”。":"In the console under “VR mode”, tap “Phone split-screen VR”: turn the phone sideways and, if you have a cardboard VR viewer, put it inside. Turn the phone to look around (drag with a finger if there is no gyroscope), tap the screen to start or stop swimming, and press “Exit VR” or Esc to return. With a VR headset, open this page in the headset’s own browser and tap “Enter headset VR”.","为了看得见而做的处理":"What we changed so you can see it","有几处为了能看清做了放大或简化：气泡放大 3 倍，珊瑚卵精束放大约 15 倍，沉船轮廓和一些生物组合是按资料示意的；这些都在规则说明里写明了。":"A few things are enlarged or simplified so they can be seen: bubbles are 3 times larger, coral egg–sperm bundles about 15 times, and the wreck outline and some animal communities are illustrative, based on sources. All of this is stated in the rules.","控制台的“地图与物理实验”里有一张全球海底地形图（真实测深数据，可以看各地点在哪里、点两点画海底剖面），还有两个独立的小实验：深海声道（声音为什么能在深海传几千公里，可以拖动声源、听远处收到的声音）和压力实验（把泡沫杯、气球、一瓶水带到海底比较）。下潜路线的进度条上也会显示挂在潜水器外的泡沫杯缩到了多大。":"Under “Map and physics experiments” in the console there is a global map of the seafloor (real bathymetry: see where each place is, or click two points to draw a seafloor profile) and two small experiments: the deep sound channel (why sound travels thousands of kilometres in the deep sea; drag the source and listen to what arrives far away) and the pressure experiment (take a foam cup, a balloon and a bottle of water to the seafloor and compare). The progress bar of the dive routes also shows how far the foam cup hanging outside the sub has shrunk.","声音":"Sound","勾选“声音”会合成浪声、呼吸和气泡声、抹香鲸的咔嗒声和深海低鸣。“物理实验”里还有深海声道的声音实验。":"Tick “Sound” to synthesise surf, breathing and bubbles, sperm whale clicks and the deep-sea rumble. “Physics experiments” also has a sound experiment on the deep sound channel.","欢迎来到海底物理世界":"Welcome to Seafloor Physics World","这里的每个场景都按真实地点和实测数据搭建，从 10 m 的珊瑚礁一直到 10,935 m 的海沟底。":"Every scene here is built from a real place and measured data, from a coral reef at 10 m all the way to the bottom of a trench at 10,935 m.","先看导览":"Watch the tour first","：“展览模式”会自动带你走过 16 个真实地点，从珊瑚礁一直下潜到海沟底，随时可以退出。":": “Exhibition mode” takes you through 16 real places automatically, from coral reefs all the way down to the bottom of the trench. You can leave at any time.","换地点":"Change place","：在右侧（手机在下方）控制台的“真实地点”里挑一个，或点“开始下潜”一路潜到海沟。":": pick one under “Real places” in the console on the right (below on phones), or press “Start dive” to dive all the way to the trench.","：拖动画面转视角，点击生物看它是谁。":": drag to turn the view, click an animal to see what it is.","自己开":"Pilot it yourself","：点“自由驾驶”，用键盘或摇杆开着水下机器人四处探索。":": press “Free piloting” and explore with an underwater robot using the keyboard or joystick.","玩点别的":"More to try","：做探险任务；在夜里或深海用手指划水，看浮游生物发光。":": take on expeditions; at night or in the deep sea, swipe your finger through the water to make plankton glow.","了解项目":"About the project","：研究思路、遗留问题和全部资料来源见":": the research approach, open issues and all sources are in the","。":".","看 8 分钟展览导览":"Watch the 8-minute tour","自己探索":"Explore on my own","看完整玩法说明":"Read the full guide","退出 VR（Esc）":"Exit VR (Esc)","这个设备不支持 WebGL，无法渲染三维场景。":"This device does not support WebGL, so the 3D scene cannot be drawn.","中文":"Chinese","浙江南麂列岛 · 岩礁潮间带":"Nanji Islands, Zhejiang · rocky intertidal","加州蒙特雷湾巨藻林":"Kelp forest, Monterey Bay, California","红海埃拉特中光层礁":"Mesophotic reef, Eilat, Red Sea","南海北部陆坡":"Northern South China Sea slope","南海海马冷泉":"Haima cold seep, South China Sea","海南陵水新村潟湖 · 海草床与红树林":"Xincun Lagoon, Lingshui, Hainan · seagrass and mangroves","太平洋克拉里昂-克利珀顿区 · 深海平原":"Clarion-Clipperton Zone, Pacific · abyssal plain","西南印度洋龙旂热液区":"Longqi vent field, Southwest Indian Ocean","蒙特雷峡谷鲸落":"Whale fall, Monterey Canyon","三沙永乐龙洞":"Yongle Blue Hole, Sansha","密克罗尼西亚特鲁克泻湖 · 富士川丸沉船":"Truk Lagoon, Micronesia · Fujikawa Maru wreck","挪威罗弗敦外海 · 勒斯特冷水珊瑚礁":"Off Lofoten, Norway · Røst cold-water coral reef","加拿大北极庞德因莱特 · 浮冰边缘":"Pond Inlet, Canadian Arctic · floe edge","加州戴维森海山 · 章鱼花园":"Davidson Seamount, California · octopus garden","南极麦克默多湾 · 海冰之下":"McMurdo Sound, Antarctica · under the sea ice","海南三亚鹿回头珊瑚礁 · 产卵之夜":"Luhuitou reef, Sanya, Hainan · spawning night","墨西哥湾 NR1 海底盐池":"NR1 brine pool, Gulf of Mexico","北太平洋副热带开阔大洋":"Open subtropical North Pacific","重走 2012 · 深海挑战者号":"Relive 2012 · Deepsea Challenger","关岛礁壁 → 马里亚纳海沟":"Guam reef wall → Mariana Trench","枝状、块状珊瑚为主，夹杂软珊瑚":"Mostly branching and massive corals, with some soft corals","块状、盘状珊瑚混生，软珊瑚增多":"Massive and plate corals mixed, more soft corals","以盘状珊瑚和软珊瑚为主":"Mostly plate corals and soft corals","太平洋沙丁鱼":"Pacific sardine","蓝绿光鳃鱼":"Blue-green chromis","丝鳍拟花鲈":"Threadfin anthias","月斑蝴蝶鱼":"Raccoon butterflyfish","眼斑双锯鱼（小丑鱼）":"Clown anemonefish (clownfish)","四线笛鲷":"Bluestripe snapper","蓝点鹦嘴鱼":"Bluebarred parrotfish","蓝平鲉":"Blue rockfish","路氏双髻鲨":"Scalloped hammerhead","银斧鱼":"Silver hatchetfish","马里亚纳狮子鱼":"Mariana snailfish","小型饵鱼":"Small baitfish","鲹":"Jack","魔鬼蓑鲉":"Red lionfish","挪威平鲉":"Norway redfish","灯笼鱼":"Lanternfish","海月水母":"Moon jellyfish","太平洋金黄水母":"Pacific sea nettle","冠水母":"Atolla jellyfish","游泳海参":"Swimming sea cucumber","栉水母":"Comb jelly","红光几乎被水吸收殆尽，身边的一切都变成了蓝绿色。":"Almost all the red light has been absorbed by the water; everything around you has turned blue-green.","200 m · 进入暮光层":"200 m · entering the twilight zone","阳光只剩不到 1%，植物无法再进行光合作用。这里的很多动物夜里会上浮到浅层觅食，这是地球上规模最大的动物迁徙。":"Less than 1% of the sunlight is left, too little for plants to photosynthesise. Many animals here rise to the shallows at night to feed: the largest animal migration on Earth.","水肺潜水的世界纪录（2014 年）。再往下，人类只能坐在耐压舱里。":"The scuba diving world record (2014). Below this, people can only go inside a pressure hull.","1,000 m · 进入午夜层":"1,000 m · entering the midnight zone","这里再也没有一丝阳光。此后看到的光，除了潜水器的灯，全部来自生物自己。":"Not a trace of sunlight is left. From here on, apart from the sub’s lights, every light you see is made by living things.","柯氏喙鲸到过这里，这是哺乳动物的下潜纪录。":"Cuvier’s beaked whales have been here: the dive record for a mammal.","约 3,700 m":"About 3,700 m","全球海洋的平均深度。地球表面七成被海水覆盖，大部分海底都在这样的黑暗里。":"The average depth of the world ocean. Seawater covers seven tenths of the Earth’s surface, and most of the seafloor lies in darkness like this.","泰坦尼克号的残骸就躺在这个深度的大西洋海底。":"The wreck of the Titanic lies on the Atlantic floor at this depth.","4,000 m · 进入深渊层":"4,000 m · entering the abyssal zone","水温约 1.5 °C，压强约 400 个大气压。几乎所有食物，都来自上方缓慢飘落的海洋雪。":"Water about 1.5 °C, pressure about 400 atmospheres. Almost all food comes from marine snow drifting slowly down from above.","6,000 m · 进入超深渊层":"6,000 m · entering the hadal zone","只存在于海沟之中。全世界的海沟加起来，还不到海底面积的 0.25%。":"Found only in trenches. All the world’s trenches together cover less than 0.25% of the seafloor.","约 8,200 m":"About 8,200 m","狮子鱼的极限。再深，鱼类体内对抗压强的分子就不够用了，这以下再也没有鱼。":"The limit for snailfish. Deeper than this, the molecules fish use to resist pressure run out, so there are no fish below here.","珠穆朗玛峰的高度。把它整个放进这条海沟，峰顶离海面还有两千多米。":"The height of Mount Everest. Put the whole mountain in this trench and its summit would still be more than two kilometres below the surface.","10,935 m · 挑战者深渊":"10,935 m · Challenger Deep","地球海洋的最深处。头顶的海水压强约 1,100 个大气压，相当于每平方厘米压着一吨多。":"The deepest point of the world ocean. The water overhead presses with about 1,100 atmospheres, more than a tonne on every square centimetre."," 小时 ":" h "," 分 ":" min "," 秒":" s","已回到水面":"Back at the surface","继续":"Continue","已到底":"On the bottom","继续下潜":"Keep diving","下潜中":"Descending","在海底":"On the seafloor","上浮中":"Ascending","2012 年 3 月 26 日 · 当地时间 ":"26 March 2012 · local time "," · 倍速 ×":" · speed ×","（真实时间的 60 倍）":" (60 × real time)","倍速 ×":"Speed ×","（在化学跃层放慢）":" (slower in the chemocline)"," · 现在：":" · Now: ","含氧层":"oxygenated layer","化学跃层，氧气迅速减少":"chemocline, oxygen dropping fast","无氧层，海水里溶有硫化氢":"anoxic layer, hydrogen sulfide in the water"," · 到洞底还有 ":" · to the bottom: ","挂在外面的泡沫杯：高度约原来的 ":"Foam cup hanging outside: about ","% · 倍速 ×":"% of its original height · speed ×","（浅处慢、空旷处快）":" (slow in the shallows, fast where it is empty)"," · 按真实速度约 1 m/s，已下潜 ":" · at the real speed of about 1 m/s you have been diving for ","，到底还要 ":", time left to the bottom: ","从关岛的礁壁出发":"Setting off from Guam’s reef wall","目标：马里亚纳海沟挑战者深渊，10,935 m。真实下潜要 3 个小时左右，可在下方调整倍速或拖动深度。":"Target: the Challenger Deep in the Mariana Trench, 10,935 m. A real dive takes about 3 hours; change the speed or drag the depth below.","造礁珊瑚":"Reef-building corals","巨藻":"Giant kelp","公主海葵":"Magnificent sea anemone","眼斑双锯鱼":"Clown anemonefish","长砗磲":"Giant clam","柳珊瑚":"Sea fan (gorgonian)","竹珊瑚":"Bamboo coral","200 m 以深":"Below 200 m","绿海龟":"Green sea turtle","阿氏前口蝠鲼":"Reef manta ray","鲸鲨":"Whale shark","紫球海胆":"Purple sea urchin","冠海胆":"Crowned sea urchin","蓝指海星":"Blue sea star","蝙蝠海星":"Bat star","各种深度":"All depths","抹香鲸":"Sperm whale","白天 200–1,200 m · 夜里上浮到表层":"200–1,200 m by day · rises to the surface at night","巨型管水母":"Giant siphonophore","大王乌贼":"Giant squid","幽灵蛸":"Vampire squid","宽咽鱼":"Gulper eel","黑鮟鱇":"Black seadevil (anglerfish)","烟灰蛸":"Dumbo octopus","偕老同穴":"Venus’ flower basket","冷泉贻贝与管栖蠕虫":"Seep mussels and tubeworms","冷泉":"Cold seeps","太平洋盲鳗":"Pacific hagfish","鲸落 · 深海":"Whale fall · deep sea","太平洋睡鲨":"Pacific sleeper shark","食骨蠕虫":"Bone-eating worm","深海石蟹":"Deep-sea king crab","盲虾":"Blind vent shrimp","印度洋热液区":"Indian Ocean vents","雪人蟹":"Yeti crab","热液区":"Hydrothermal vents","鳞角腹足蜗牛（铁甲蜗牛）":"Scaly-foot snail","盾巨螺":"Giant vent snail","西南印度洋热液区":"Southwest Indian Ocean vents","印度洋深海偏顶蛤":"Indian Ocean deep-sea mussel","柄藤壶":"Stalked barnacle","热液区外圈":"Outer ring of the vent field","深海海葵":"Deep-sea anemone","鹿角珊瑚（产卵中）":"Staghorn coral (spawning)","0–30 m · 每年集体产卵":"0–30 m · mass spawning once a year","软珊瑚":"Soft coral","Dendronephthya 等":"Dendronephthya and others","0–50 m · 沉船与礁石":"0–50 m · wrecks and reefs","小型饵鱼群":"School of small baitfish","Atherinidae 等":"Atherinidae and others","热带浅海":"Tropical shallow seas","0–50 m · 印度—太平洋":"0–50 m · Indo-Pacific","深水石珊瑚（佩尔图萨珊瑚）":"Deep-water stony coral (Desmophyllum pertusum)","泡泡糖珊瑚":"Bubblegum coral","冷水 · 200–1,300 m":"Cold water · 200–1,300 m","北大西洋 · 100–1,000 m":"North Atlantic · 100–1,000 m","球海绵":"Geodia sponge","北大西洋深海":"Deep North Atlantic","大锉蛤":"Giant file clam","威德尔海豹":"Weddell seal","南极海冰下":"Under the Antarctic sea ice","冰鱼（白血鱼）":"Icefish (white-blooded fish)","南大洋 · −1.8–2 °C":"Southern Ocean · −1.8–2 °C","秃南极鱼":"Bald notothen","南极海冰底下":"Underside of the Antarctic sea ice","冰藻":"Ice algae","海冰底部的硅藻群落":"Diatom communities on the underside of sea ice","南北极海冰底部":"Underside of Arctic and Antarctic sea ice","南极红海星":"Antarctic red sea star","南大洋":"Southern Ocean","南极海胆":"Antarctic sea urchin","巨型海蜘蛛":"Giant sea spider","南大洋海底":"Southern Ocean seafloor","南极玻璃海绵":"Antarctic glass sponge","墨西哥湾甲烷贻贝":"Gulf of Mexico methane mussel","墨西哥湾冷泉 · 盐池岸边":"Gulf of Mexico seeps · brine pool shores","磷虾":"Krill","0–500 m · 每天上下迁移":"0–500 m · migrates up and down every day","樽海鞘":"Salp","0–800 m · 每天上下迁移":"0–800 m · migrates up and down every day","巨型钩虾":"Giant amphipod","海沟底部":"Trench floor","超深渊海参":"Hadal sea cucumber","巨型单细胞生物":"Giant single-celled organism (xenophyophore)","已遇见 ":"Met "," 位探险者遇见过\">":" explorers have met it\">","人</b>":" met</b>","<span class=\"sp unk\">？？？<i>":"<span class=\"sp unk\">???<i>","任务完成：":"Expedition complete: ","新遇见：":"New sighting: ","声音：":"Sound: ","开":"on","关":"off","潜水纪录":"Diving record","阳光消失":"Sunlight gone","平均深度 · 泰坦尼克":"Average depth · Titanic","海沟":"Trench","鱼类极限":"Fish limit","\" class=\"pl\">珠峰 8,849 m</text>":"\" class=\"pl\">Everest 8,849 m</text>","2012 年 3 月 26 日 05:15":"26 March 2012, 05:15","关岛西南约 330 km。詹姆斯·卡梅隆独自驾驶 12 吨重的“深海挑战者号”离开水面。潜水器竖着下潜，驾驶舱是一个只容一人蜷坐的钢球。":"About 330 km south-west of Guam. James Cameron leaves the surface alone in the 12-tonne Deepsea Challenger. The sub dives upright; its cockpit is a steel sphere just big enough for one person curled up.","舱内像桑拿":"Like a sauna inside","下潜初期舱内温度一度超过 38 °C；越往下，舱外海水越冷，最后只有 2 °C 左右。":"Early in the dive the cabin passed 38 °C; deeper down the water outside grew colder, finally only about 2 °C.","07:51 抵达海底":"07:51 · reaches the bottom","下潜用了 2 小时 36 分。公布的深度在 10,843 至 10,908 m 之间。巨大的压强让整艘潜水器缩短了约 7.6 cm。":"The descent took 2 h 36 min. Published depths range from 10,843 to 10,908 m. The enormous pressure shortened the whole sub by about 7.6 cm.","“荒凉、孤寂，像月球一样的平原”":"“Desolate, isolated, a lunar-like plain”","卡梅隆说他就坐在那里看着窗外。海底是柔软得近乎胶状的平地，几乎没有任何起伏。":"Cameron said he just sat there looking out of the window. The bottom was soft, almost gelatinous, and nearly flat.","没有鱼":"No fish","除了不到 2.5 cm 长、像小虾一样的端足类，他没有看到任何更大的动物。":"Apart from shrimp-like amphipods less than 2.5 cm long, he saw no larger animals.","液压油泄漏":"Hydraulic leak","正要采集第一份样本时，液压油泄漏糊住了舷窗，机械臂无法使用，几个推进器也失灵了。":"Just as he was about to take the first sample, leaking hydraulic fluid smeared the viewport, the robot arm stopped working and several thrusters failed.","提前上浮":"Early ascent","在海底停留了三个多小时（原计划 6 小时）。1960 年，沃尔什和皮卡德在这里只停留了 20 分钟。":"He stayed on the bottom for just over three hours (6 were planned). In 1960, Walsh and Piccard stayed here for only 20 minutes.","约 12:00 回到水面":"About 12:00 · back at the surface","上浮只用了 70 分钟。卡梅隆是第一个独自到达挑战者深渊的人，也是 1960 年之后第一个到达这里的人。":"The ascent took only 70 minutes. Cameron was the first person to reach the Challenger Deep alone, and the first to reach it since 1960."," 周":" weeks"," 个月":" months"," 年":" years","食腐动物阶段：盲鳗和睡鲨在啃食鲸肉，每天能吃掉 40–60 kg。":"Scavenger stage: hagfish and sleeper sharks are eating the whale’s flesh, up to 40–60 kg a day.","机会主义者阶段：骨头露出，红色的食骨蠕虫把“根”钻进骨头里。":"Opportunist stage: the bones are exposed, and red bone-eating worms push their “roots” into them.","化能合成阶段：细菌分解骨头里的油脂，放出硫化氢，白色细菌席和贻贝靠它生活，可以持续几十年。":"Chemosynthetic stage: bacteria break down the oil in the bones and release hydrogen sulfide; white bacterial mats and mussels live on it, for decades.","黑烟囱":"Black smoker","热液喷口 · 约 6 m 高":"Hydrothermal vent · about 6 m tall","海水从海底裂缝渗下去，被岩浆加热到 300 多摄氏度，溶进铁、铜、锌等金属后从这里喷出；一碰到 2 °C 的海水，金属硫化物瞬间析出，就成了“黑烟”。这里压强约 280 个大气压，海水要到约 400 °C 才会沸腾，所以热液不会沸腾。":"Seawater seeps down through cracks in the seafloor, is heated by magma to more than 300 °C, dissolves iron, copper, zinc and other metals, and gushes out here; the moment it meets 2 °C seawater, metal sulfides precipitate as “black smoke”. The pressure here is about 280 atmospheres, and seawater would not boil until about 400 °C, so the vent fluid never boils.","如意金箍棒":"Ruyi Jingu Bang","硫化物柱 · 20 m 以上":"Sulfide spire · over 20 m","龙旂热液区里一根 20 多米高的硫化物柱，科考队给它起了这个名字。烟囱由析出的硫化物一层层堆起来，这么高说明这里的喷发已经持续了很久。":"A sulfide spire more than 20 m tall in the Longqi vent field; the survey team named it after the Monkey King’s magic staff. Chimneys build up layer by layer from precipitated sulfides, so this height means the venting has gone on for a long time.","九头蛇（Hydra）":"Hydra","一圈六根小烟囱 · 约 2 m 高":"A ring of six small chimneys · about 2 m tall","六根小烟囱围成一圈。年轻的黑烟囱上以盲虾和铁甲蜗牛为主，老一些、只剩弥散流的烟囱则被巨螺、贻贝和藤壶占据。":"Six small chimneys stand in a ring. Young black smokers are dominated by blind shrimp and scaly-foot snails; older chimneys with only diffuse flow are taken over by giant snails, mussels and barnacles.","弥散流烟囱":"Diffuse-flow chimney","温度较低的热液慢慢渗出":"Cooler vent fluid seeping slowly","这里没有黑烟，较凉的热液从岩体缝隙里渗出，外围长满了巨螺和贻贝。":"No black smoke here: cooler fluid seeps from cracks in the rock, and the outside is covered in giant snails and mussels.","海冰底面与冰藻":"Underside of the sea ice, with ice algae","海冰厚约 2 m · 水温 −1.9 °C":"Sea ice about 2 m thick · water −1.9 °C","阳光穿过约 2 m 厚的海冰和积雪后只剩百分之几，冰底那些褐色的斑块是冰藻：硅藻等微藻生活在海冰底部和下方松散的“片状冰”里，靠这一点点光进行光合作用，是南极磷虾等动物的重要食物。":"After passing through about 2 m of sea ice and snow, only a few percent of the sunlight is left. The brown patches on the underside are ice algae: diatoms and other microalgae living in the bottom of the ice and in the loose “platelet ice” below it, photosynthesising with this little light. They are an important food for Antarctic krill and other animals.","南极麦克默多湾":"McMurdo Sound, Antarctica","卵精束":"Egg–sperm bundle","直径约 1–2 mm · 画面中放大约 15 倍":"About 1–2 mm across · drawn about 15 times larger","一个卵精束里裹着几十粒卵和成千上万个精子。卵富含脂质，比海水轻，所以卵精束会上浮；到水面后约一小时内散开，卵才和来自其他珊瑚的精子相遇。同一珊瑚自己的卵和精子大多不能互相受精。":"Each bundle wraps dozens of eggs and thousands of sperm. The eggs are rich in lipids and lighter than seawater, so the bundles float up; within about an hour of reaching the surface they break apart, and the eggs meet sperm from other corals. A coral’s own eggs and sperm mostly cannot fertilise each other.","盐池的“湖面”":"The brine pool’s “lake surface”","卤水与海水的分界面 · 水深约 650 m":"Boundary between brine and seawater · about 650 m deep","这里的卤水含盐量约为海水的 4 倍，密度约 1.09 g/cm³，比海水重，所以沉在海底聚成一个“湖”，有清晰的湖面和湖岸，不和上面的海水混合。两层水密度只差约 6%，湖面波浪的回复力只有普通水面的约 3%，1 米长的波要 4–5 秒才起伏一次。你刚才碰到的地方会慢慢荡开一圈波纹。潜水器可以像船一样“停”在这个湖面上。":"The brine here is about 4 times as salty as seawater, with a density of about 1.09 g/cm³. It is heavier than seawater, so it sinks and pools on the seafloor as a “lake” with a clear surface and shore, not mixing with the water above. The two layers differ in density by only about 6%, so the restoring force on the waves is only about 3% of a normal water surface, and a 1 m wave takes 4–5 seconds to rise and fall. Ripples spread slowly from the spot you just touched. A submersible can “float” on this lake surface like a boat.","墨西哥湾 NR1 盐池":"NR1 brine pool, Gulf of Mexico","误入卤水的动物":"Animals that strayed into the brine","盐池底部":"Bottom of the brine pool","卤水几乎不含氧气，盐度又极高，游进或掉进去的动物很快就会死去，被卤水“腌”着保存下来。墨西哥湾另一个水深约 1,000 m 的盐池因此被叫作“绝望按摩池”（Jacuzzi of Despair），池边散落着这样的螃蟹和鱼。":"The brine holds almost no oxygen and is extremely salty, so animals that swim or fall in soon die and are “pickled” in it. Another brine pool in the Gulf of Mexico, about 1,000 m deep, is called the “Jacuzzi of Despair” for this reason, with crabs and fish like these scattered along its edge.","不再活动的硫化物烟囱":"Inactive sulfide chimney","只剩矿物":"Only minerals left","热液已经停止，烟囱外层被氧化成铁锈色，柄藤壶和海葵在上面安家。龙旂热液区至少有 13 座这样不再活动的大型硫化物堆积体。":"The venting has stopped and the outside of the chimney has oxidised to rust; stalked barnacles and anemones have settled on it. The Longqi vent field has at least 13 large inactive sulfide mounds like this.","清晨":"Early morning","傍晚":"Late afternoon","黎明":"Dawn","黄昏":"Dusk","夜里":"Night","停在那里":"holding still","正以约 ":"moving at about "," m/min 上升":" m/min upwards"," m/min 下沉":" m/min downwards","</b> · 水面光照约为正午的 ":"</b> · surface light is about ","。灯笼鱼层在约 <b>":" of noon. The lanternfish layer is at about <b>"," m</b>，":" m</b>, ","；磷虾层约 ":"; the krill layer is at about "," m，樽海鞘约 ":" m and salps at about "," m。银斧鱼不迁移，一直留在 300–500 m。":" m. Hatchetfish do not migrate and stay at 300–500 m.","地球上规模最大的迁移":"The largest migration on Earth","每天黄昏，暮光层里数以十亿计的灯笼鱼、磷虾和樽海鞘从几百米深处升到表层觅食，天亮前再沉回去。你现在悬停在 ":"Every evening, billions of lanternfish, krill and salps in the twilight zone rise from hundreds of metres down to feed near the surface, and sink again before dawn. You are hovering at "," m，看着它们到来。":" m, watching them arrive.","13 m · 温跃层":"13 m · thermocline","往下水温开始降低。洞口附近的珊瑚和二十多种鱼都生活在上面这几十米里。":"Below here the water starts to cool. The corals near the mouth and more than twenty kinds of fish live in these top few tens of metres.","70 m · 进入化学跃层":"70 m · entering the chemocline","氧气开始迅速减少。洞里的水几乎不和外面的海水交换，下层的氧气一旦用完就得不到补充。":"Oxygen starts to fall quickly. The water in the hole barely exchanges with the open sea, so once the oxygen in the lower layers is used up it is never replaced.","约 77 m · 洞道转折":"About 77 m · the shaft turns","龙洞的形状像一只芭蕾舞鞋：在 76–78 m 和约 158 m 处各有一次大的转折。":"The blue hole is shaped like a ballet shoe, with two big bends at 76–78 m and at about 158 m.","100 m · 氧气耗尽":"100 m · oxygen runs out","从这里往下，海水里没有溶解氧，却富含硫化氢。鱼、藻类都无法生存，只剩下微生物。":"Below here the water has no dissolved oxygen but plenty of hydrogen sulfide. Neither fish nor algae can survive; only microbes are left.","约 100–150 m · 浑浊的细菌层":"About 100–150 m · cloudy bacterial layer","硫氧化细菌在 100–140 m 占到微生物的约九成，悬浮的有机颗粒在约 150 m 最多，海水在这里发浑。":"Sulfur-oxidising bacteria make up about 90% of the microbes at 100–140 m, and suspended organic particles peak at about 150 m, so the water turns cloudy here.","约 158 m · 第二次转折":"About 158 m · the second bend","再往下是均匀、静止、无氧的老水，水温稳定在约 15 °C。":"Below is uniform, still, oxygen-free old water, holding steady at about 15 °C.","约 301 m · 龙洞底部":"About 301 m · bottom of the blue hole","2016 年测得 300.89 m，是当时已知最深的蓝洞（现已知墨西哥的 Taam Ja' 蓝洞至少 420 m）。洞底沉积的有机碳最老约 6,800 年。":"Measured at 300.89 m in 2016, then the deepest known blue hole (Taam Ja’ in Mexico is now known to be at least 420 m). The oldest organic carbon in its bottom sediment is about 6,800 years old.","含氧":"Oxygenated","化学跃层":"Chemocline","浑浊细菌层":"Cloudy bacterial layer","无氧 · 硫化氢":"Anoxic · hydrogen sulfide","约 301 m":"About 301 m","西沙永乐环礁上的一口海底竖井，深约 301 m，洞口宽约 130 m。上面几十米是热闹的珊瑚礁，100 m 以下的海水里没有氧气。":"A seafloor shaft on Yongle Atoll in the Paracels, about 301 m deep with a mouth about 130 m wide. The top few tens of metres are a busy coral reef; below 100 m the water has no oxygen.","<b>“含卵”</b>：珊瑚虫把卵精束顶到口部，整块珊瑚表面布满粉红色的小点，随时准备释放。":"<b>“Setting”</b>: the polyps push their egg–sperm bundles up to their mouths, and the whole coral is dotted with pink, ready to release.","<b>释放</b>：鹿角珊瑚一丛接一丛地放出卵精束。每个卵精束直径约 1–2 mm，里面裹着几十粒卵和成千上万个精子，因为卵富含脂质，比海水轻，便慢慢往上飘。":"<b>Release</b>: one Acropora colony after another lets go of its bundles. Each bundle is about 1–2 mm across and wraps dozens of eggs and thousands of sperm; the eggs are rich in lipids and lighter than seawater, so the bundle drifts slowly upwards.","<b>上浮</b>：卵精束以约每秒 1 cm 的速度上升，几分钟就能到达水面，在那里散开，卵和其他珊瑚的精子相遇受精。受精窗口只有约 2 小时。":"<b>Rising</b>: the bundles rise at about 1 cm per second and reach the surface within minutes, where they break apart and the eggs meet sperm from other corals. The window for fertilisation is only about 2 hours.","<b>浮层</b>：水面聚起一层粉红色的卵层。接下来几天，受精卵发育成幼虫，随海流漂走，再找一块礁石定居。":"<b>Slick</b>: a pink layer of eggs gathers at the surface. Over the next few days the fertilised eggs develop into larvae, drift away on the currents and look for a reef to settle on."," 已释放约 ":" About "," 个卵精束（画面中放大约 15 倍显示）。":" bundles released so far (drawn about 15 times larger).","富士川丸":"Fujikawa Maru","日本海军飞机运输舰 · 长 133 m · 1944 年沉没":"Japanese navy aircraft transport · 133 m long · sunk in 1944","1938 年建成的货船，后被日本海军征用来运输飞机。1944 年 2 月 17–18 日，美军航母舰载机对特鲁克泻湖发动“冰雹行动”，击沉 45 艘以上的舰船、摧毁近 300 架飞机，富士川丸被鱼雷击中后沉没。它直立着坐在约 34 m 深的沙底上，八十多年后成了一座人工鱼礁。":"A cargo ship built in 1938 and later requisitioned by the Japanese navy to carry aircraft. On 17–18 February 1944, US carrier aircraft attacked Truk Lagoon in Operation Hailstone, sinking more than 45 ships and destroying nearly 300 aircraft; the Fujikawa Maru was hit by a torpedo and sank. It sits upright on sand about 34 m deep and, more than eighty years later, has become an artificial reef.","特鲁克泻湖":"Truk Lagoon","货舱里的战斗机":"Fighter planes in the hold","2 号货舱 · 拆解状态":"Hold No. 2 · dismantled","前部货舱里至今躺着至少 9 架拆解的日本战斗机，其中 8 架是零式，另有 1 架是现存唯一的九六式舰载战斗机。":"The forward hold still holds at least 9 dismantled Japanese fighters: 8 Zeros and the only surviving Type 96 carrier fighter.","珊瑚虫体内住着虫黄藻，靠光合作用为珊瑚提供大部分能量，所以造礁珊瑚只能活在有光的浅海。":"Coral polyps host zooxanthellae, algae that photosynthesise and supply most of the coral’s energy, so reef-building corals can only live in sunlit shallow seas.","每天最快能长约 60 cm，是地球上长得最快的生物之一；叶片基部的气囊让它漂向水面。":"It can grow up to about 60 cm a day, one of the fastest-growing living things on Earth; gas bladders at the base of each blade float it towards the surface.","触手上的刺细胞能蜇伤小鱼，但小丑鱼体表的黏液让它们不会被蜇。":"Stinging cells on its tentacles can sting small fish, but the mucus on a clownfish’s skin keeps it from being stung.","一群小丑鱼里最大的那条是雌鱼；雌鱼不在了，最大的雄鱼会变成雌鱼。":"The largest clownfish in a group is the female; if she disappears, the largest male turns into a female.","外套膜里养着共生藻，像珊瑚一样靠阳光获得营养；那片蓝色来自会反光的虹彩细胞。":"Its mantle holds symbiotic algae, so like corals it gets food from sunlight; the blue comes from iridescent cells that reflect light.","扇面垂直于海流生长，好拦截更多随水流来的浮游食物。":"The fan grows across the current to catch more of the plankton carried past.","骨骼一节白一节深，像竹子；可以活几百年，被触碰时会发出蓝色光波。":"Its skeleton alternates white and dark segments like bamboo; it can live for hundreds of years and sends out a wave of blue light when touched.","名字里的“绿”来自体内脂肪的颜色，因为成年后主要吃海草和藻类。":"The “green” in its name comes from the colour of its body fat, because adults eat mainly seagrass and algae.","翼展可达 5 m，脑与体型之比在鱼类中名列前茅。":"Its wingspan can reach 5 m, and its brain-to-body ratio is among the highest of any fish.","世界上最大的鱼，可长到 18 m 以上，却只吃浮游生物和小鱼。":"The largest fish in the world, growing to more than 18 m, yet it eats only plankton and small fish.","锤状的头部布满电感受器，像金属探测器一样扫描海底找猎物；白天常成百上千地聚群。":"Its hammer-shaped head is packed with electroreceptors that sweep the seafloor for prey like a metal detector; by day they often gather in schools of hundreds.","遇到危险时会一起钻进枝状珊瑚的缝隙里。":"When threatened, the whole group dives into the gaps of branching corals.","群体里大多是雌鱼；雄鱼不在了，雌鱼会变性成雄鱼。":"Most of a group are females; if the male disappears, a female changes sex to become the male.","眼睛藏在黑色条纹里，尾部的黑斑像假眼睛，用来迷惑捕食者。":"Its eye hides in a black stripe, and a dark spot near the tail acts as a false eye to confuse predators.","白天成群停在珊瑚礁旁，夜里散开去觅食。":"By day they hover in schools beside the reef; at night they scatter to feed.","啃食珊瑚上的藻类时连骨骼一起咬碎，排出的就是细白沙；热带海滩的白沙很多来自鹦嘴鱼。":"When it scrapes algae off coral it bites the skeleton too, and what comes out is fine white sand; much of the white sand on tropical beaches comes from parrotfish.","遇到捕食者时会挤成旋转的“鱼饵球”，让捕食者难以锁定某一条。":"Faced with a predator, sardines pack into a swirling “bait ball” so it is hard to single out any one fish.","可以活 40 多年，常在巨藻林中层成群悬停。":"It can live for more than 40 years and often hovers in schools in the middle of the kelp forest.","数量失控时会把巨藻林啃成光秃秃的“海胆荒漠”，海獭是它们的主要天敌。":"When their numbers get out of control they graze kelp forests bare into “urchin barrens”; sea otters are their main predator.","细长的刺带有微毒，白天躲着，夜里出来啃食藻类。":"Its long, thin spines are mildly venomous; it hides by day and comes out at night to graze algae.","断掉的一条腕能长成一只完整的新海星。":"A single arm that breaks off can grow into a whole new sea star.","几乎什么都吃，会把胃翻出体外消化食物。":"It eats almost anything, turning its stomach inside out to digest food outside its body.","伞中央四个马蹄形的是生殖腺；生命中有一段固着在岩石上的水螅体阶段。":"The four horseshoe shapes in the middle of the bell are its gonads; part of its life is spent as a polyp attached to rock.","触手可长到 4 m 以上，布满刺细胞，用来捕捉浮游动物。":"Its tentacles can grow more than 4 m long, covered in stinging cells for catching zooplankton.","靠八列纤毛栉板划水，是用纤毛游泳的最大动物；彩虹色是纤毛衍射光线，不是发光。":"It rows with eight rows of comb plates made of cilia, the largest animal to swim with cilia; the rainbow is light diffracted by the cilia, not light it makes.","有地球上最大的大脑（约 8 kg），能潜到 2,000 m 以下捕食大型乌贼，靠咔嗒声回声定位。":"It has the largest brain on Earth (about 8 kg), dives below 2,000 m to hunt large squid, and finds them by echolocation clicks.","可能是数量最多的脊椎动物之一；夜里上浮到表层觅食，白天回到几百米深处。":"Possibly among the most numerous vertebrates; it rises to the surface at night to feed and returns to hundreds of metres down by day.","腹部的发光器发出和上方透下来一样亮的光，把自己的影子“抹掉”，这叫反照明。":"Photophores on its belly glow as brightly as the light filtering down from above, “erasing” its shadow; this is called counterillumination.","看起来像一只动物，其实是许多分工不同的个体连成的群体，有的长达数十米。":"It looks like one animal but is a colony of many individuals with different jobs, some tens of metres long.","眼睛直径约 27 cm，是动物界最大的眼睛之一；2012 年才第一次在自然环境中被拍到活体。":"Its eye is about 27 cm across, one of the largest in the animal kingdom; a live one was filmed in the wild for the first time only in 2012.","名字吓人，其实吃的是“海洋雪”；受威胁时会把披风般的腕翻过来罩住身体。":"Despite the scary name it eats “marine snow”; when threatened it turns its cloak-like arms inside out over its body.","被攻击时让光沿伞缘一圈圈旋转闪烁，像防盗警报，可能招来更大的捕食者对付攻击者。你刚才点它，就相当于“碰”了它一下。":"When attacked it sends light spinning around the rim of its bell like a burglar alarm, perhaps to attract a bigger predator to deal with the attacker. Clicking it just now was like “bumping” it.","嘴能张得比身体还大，尾端有发光器，可能用来引诱猎物。":"Its mouth can open wider than its body, and the tip of its tail has a light organ that may lure prey.","能离开海底游泳的海参，身体半透明，能看见里面的消化道。":"A sea cucumber that can leave the seafloor and swim; its body is translucent, so you can see its gut inside.","头上“钓竿”末端住着发光细菌；在一些鮟鱇物种里，雄鱼会咬住雌鱼并和它长在一起。":"Glowing bacteria live at the tip of the “fishing rod” on its head; in some anglerfish species the male bites onto the female and fuses with her.","像大象耳朵的鳍是主要推进器；曾在近 7,000 m 深处被拍到，是已知最深的章鱼之一。":"Its fins, like elephant ears, are its main propulsion; it has been filmed nearly 7,000 m deep, among the deepest octopuses known.","玻璃般的骨骼由二氧化硅构成；常有一对小虾幼年钻进去，长大后出不来，在里面过完一生。":"Its glassy skeleton is made of silica; often a pair of young shrimp crawl inside, grow too big to get out, and spend their whole lives there.","不靠阳光，靠体内共生细菌把甲烷或硫化物转化成能量。":"It does not rely on sunlight: symbiotic bacteria in its body turn methane or sulfide into energy.","身体柔软半透明，骨骼没有完全钙化，能承受 800 多个大气压。":"Its body is soft and translucent and its skeleton not fully calcified, so it can withstand more than 800 atmospheres.","体内有能分解纤维素的酶，可能靠从陆地漂来、沉入海沟的植物残骸生活。":"It has enzymes that break down cellulose and may live on plant remains washed from land that sink into the trench.","海沟底部数量最多的大型动物之一，不停吞食沉积物，吸收里面的有机物。":"Among the most numerous large animals on the trench floor, it swallows sediment non-stop and absorbs the organic matter in it.","单个细胞可以长到 10 cm 以上，是已知最大的单细胞生物之一。":"A single cell can grow larger than 10 cm, one of the largest single-celled organisms known.","受惊时几秒钟内就能分泌出大量黏液，连鲨鱼的鳃都能堵住；会钻进腐肉里从内部吃起。":"When startled it can release masses of slime within seconds, enough to clog even a shark’s gills; it burrows into carcasses and eats them from the inside.","游得很慢的冷水鲨鱼，能长到 4 m 以上，常在鲸落上撕咬鲸肉。":"A slow-swimming cold-water shark that can grow beyond 4 m, often seen tearing flesh from whale falls.","没有嘴也没有肠子，靠“根”分泌酸钻进鲸骨，再借共生细菌消化骨头里的营养；2002 年在蒙特雷峡谷 2,893 m 的灰鲸骨头上首次被发现。":"It has no mouth and no gut: its “roots” secrete acid to bore into whale bone, and symbiotic bacteria digest the nutrients in the bone; first discovered in 2002 on grey whale bones at 2,893 m in Monterey Canyon.","被腐肉的气味吸引而来的甲壳动物之一，会在骨头之间翻找残渣。":"One of the crustaceans drawn by the smell of carrion, picking through the scraps between the bones.","没有普通的眼睛，背上却有一块感光器官，科学家认为它可能用来感知热液口发出的极微弱的光；靠体内和鳃腔里的共生细菌获取养分。":"It has no ordinary eyes, but a light-sensitive organ on its back that scientists think may sense the extremely faint glow of the vents; it gets food from symbiotic bacteria in its body and gill chambers.","俗称“雪人蟹”，螯足上长满刚毛，上面养着细菌；龙旂的这一种是在这里首次发现的新种。":"Known as the “yeti crab”, its claws are covered in bristles that farm bacteria; the species at Longqi was discovered here as new to science.","脚上覆盖着数百片含硫化铁的鳞片，壳的外层也含硫化铁，是已知唯一把铁硫化物用进骨骼的动物；靠体内的共生细菌生活。2019 年被列为濒危，是第一种因深海采矿威胁而被列为濒危的物种。":"Its foot is covered in hundreds of scales containing iron sulfide, and the outer layer of its shell has iron sulfide too, the only animal known to build iron sulfides into its skeleton; it lives on symbiotic bacteria in its body. Listed as endangered in 2019, it was the first species listed because of the threat of deep-sea mining.","和铁甲蜗牛是近亲的大型热液螺，同样靠体内的共生细菌生活，在龙旂成片分布，2015 年才被命名。":"A large vent snail closely related to the scaly-foot snail, also living on symbiotic bacteria in its body; it covers large patches at Longqi and was named only in 2015.","鳃里住着共生细菌，把热液里的化学能转化成养分，在喷口外围成片生长。":"Symbiotic bacteria in its gills turn the chemical energy of the vent fluid into food; it grows in patches around the outside of the vents.","长在热液影响的最外圈，伸出羽状的蔓足从水里滤食。":"It lives in the outermost ring influenced by the vents, sweeping feathery legs through the water to filter food.","没有坚硬骨骼的珊瑚，靠水压撑起身体，喜欢长在水流经过的高处，所以沉船的桅杆、吊杆和栏杆上挂满了它们，颜色从粉红、淡紫到橙红都有。":"Soft corals have no hard skeleton and are held up by water pressure. They like high spots where the current flows, so the wreck’s masts, booms and railings are covered with them, in colours from pink and lilac to orange-red.","成千上万的小鱼在甲板上方结成密集的鱼群，一起转向来迷惑捕食者。":"Thousands of small fish form tight schools above the deck and turn together to confuse predators.","在沉船边缘巡游的掠食者，时不时冲进饵鱼群里捕食。":"A predator patrolling the edge of the wreck, now and then charging into the baitfish school to feed.","鳍条上长着毒刺，动作缓慢，常在沉船船尾的阴影里伏击小鱼。它们原产印度—太平洋，在大西洋已成为严重的入侵物种。":"Venomous spines grow on its fin rays; it moves slowly and often ambushes small fish in the shadow of the stern. Native to the Indo-Pacific, it has become a serious invasive species in the Atlantic.","深水里最重要的造礁珊瑚。它没有共生藻，靠伸出触手捕食浮游生物，所以能活在没有阳光的冷水里；有白色和橙色两种颜色型。每年只长 1–2.5 mm 左右，礁体底部是层层堆积的死珊瑚骨架，只有顶端是活的。底拖网曾毁掉挪威大陆架约三到五成的珊瑚区。":"The most important reef-building coral in deep water. It has no symbiotic algae and catches plankton with its tentacles, so it can live in cold water without sunlight; it comes in white and orange colour forms. It grows only about 1–2.5 mm a year; the base of the reef is layer upon layer of dead coral skeleton, and only the tips are alive. Bottom trawling once destroyed about 30–50% of the coral areas on the Norwegian shelf.","一种长成小树的大型柳珊瑚，枝端圆鼓鼓的，像嚼过的泡泡糖，因此得名。颜色从白色到鲜红都有，能长到几米高。":"A large gorgonian that grows into a small tree, its branch tips rounded like chewed bubblegum, hence the name. Colours range from white to bright red, and it can grow several metres tall.","北大西洋深水里的大眼红鱼，常静静悬停在冷水珊瑚礁上方。它们长得很慢、寿命很长，有的能活几十年以上。":"A big-eyed red fish of the deep North Atlantic, often hovering quietly above cold-water coral reefs. They grow slowly and live long, some for many decades.","大块的球形海绵，内部有硅质骨针，是北大西洋深海“海绵场”的主角，为许多小动物提供栖身之所。":"A large ball-shaped sponge with silica spicules inside, the star of the deep North Atlantic “sponge grounds”, giving shelter to many small animals.","贝壳可长到十几厘米的大型锉蛤，常附着在冷水珊瑚的骨架上，张开的壳缘伸出一圈橙色的触手。":"A large file clam whose shell can reach over ten centimetres, often attached to cold-water coral skeletons, with a ring of orange tentacles reaching out from its open shell.","世界上最南端的哺乳动物之一，整个冬天都待在海冰下。它们用牙齿啃磨冰面来维持呼吸孔，成年个体约 400 kg，在冰下捕食南极鱼。":"One of the southernmost mammals in the world, it spends the whole winter under the sea ice. It keeps its breathing holes open by grinding the ice with its teeth; adults weigh about 400 kg and hunt Antarctic fish under the ice.","已知唯一成年后血液里没有血红蛋白的脊椎动物，血液几乎无色。氧气直接溶解在血浆里运输，靠的是冰冷海水溶氧多、心脏和血量都比别的鱼大好几倍。":"The only vertebrate known to have no haemoglobin in its blood as an adult, so its blood is almost colourless. Oxygen is carried dissolved in the plasma, which works because icy water holds plenty of oxygen and its heart and blood volume are several times larger than other fish.","躲在海冰底下的片状冰层里生活，血液里有抗冻糖蛋白，能在 −1.9 °C 的海水里不被冻住。":"It lives in the platelet ice under the sea ice; antifreeze glycoproteins in its blood keep it from freezing in −1.9 °C water.","生活在海冰底部的微藻，春季冰下光照回升时大量繁殖，把冰底染成褐色，是南北两极食物网的起点之一。":"Microalgae living on the underside of sea ice. When light under the ice returns in spring they bloom and stain the ice brown; they are one of the starting points of the food webs at both poles.","南极海底最常见的海星之一，颜色鲜红，什么都吃，包括海豹的粪便。":"One of the most common sea stars on the Antarctic seafloor, bright red, eating anything, including seal droppings.","南极浅海最常见的海胆，常成堆聚集；冬天会被海底的“锚冰”冻住带离海底。":"The most common sea urchin in shallow Antarctic waters, often in heaps; in winter they can be frozen into “anchor ice” and carried off the seafloor.","海蜘蛛不是蜘蛛，而是一类海洋节肢动物。南极的海蜘蛛长得特别大，腿展可达几十厘米，这种“极地巨型化”可能与冷水含氧多有关。":"Sea spiders are not spiders but a group of marine arthropods. Antarctic sea spiders grow especially large, with legs spanning tens of centimetres; this “polar gigantism” may be linked to the high oxygen content of cold water.","南极浅海的玻璃海绵，骨骼由二氧化硅骨针构成。它们长得极慢，有的个体可能已有上千岁。":"A glass sponge of shallow Antarctic waters, with a skeleton of silica spicules. They grow extremely slowly; some individuals may be more than a thousand years old.","造礁珊瑚里种类最多的一属。大多数鹿角珊瑚雌雄同体，每年只在少数几个夜里把卵和精子一起包成卵精束放出，在水里与其他珊瑚的配子相遇受精。":"The most species-rich genus of reef-building corals. Most Acropora are hermaphrodites that, on just a few nights a year, release eggs and sperm packed together into bundles, which meet gametes from other corals in the water to be fertilised.","鳃里住着以甲烷为食的共生细菌，细菌再把养分供给贻贝。它们沿盐池的“湖岸”长成一圈：往里是没有氧气的卤水，往外甲烷又不够，只有岸边两样都有。":"Symbiotic bacteria that feed on methane live in its gills and pass nutrients to the mussel. They grow in a ring along the brine pool’s “shore”: inside is oxygen-free brine, outside there is too little methane; only the shore has both.","身上有一排排会发蓝光的发光器。白天躲在几百米深的暗处，黄昏上浮到表层吃浮游植物，天亮前再沉回去。":"It has rows of photophores that glow blue. By day it hides in the dark hundreds of metres down; at dusk it rises to the surface to eat plankton, and sinks again before dawn.","一个个透明的“小桶”连成长链，靠喷水前进，边游边滤食。它们每天要上下迁移几百米，粪粒沉得很快，把碳带进深海。":"Transparent “barrels” linked in long chains, moving by jet propulsion and filtering food as they swim. They migrate hundreds of metres up and down every day, and their faecal pellets sink fast, carrying carbon into the deep sea.","住在热液区最外缘，那里水温已接近周围海水，食物却比普通深海海底丰富得多。":"It lives on the outermost edge of the vent field, where the water is almost as cold as the surrounding sea but food is far richer than on the ordinary deep seafloor.","龙旂热液区":"Longqi vent field"," · 距离你约 ":" · distance about ","灰鲸遗骸":"Grey whale carcass","沉到海底 ":"On the seafloor for ","约 13 m 长 · 骨头里储存着上千公斤油脂":"About 13 m long · its bones hold more than a tonne of oil","一头鲸沉到深海后，能养活一个群落几十年。科学家已在鲸落上记录到 400 多种生物，其中至少 30 种在别处从未见过。":"A whale that sinks to the deep sea can feed a community for decades. Scientists have recorded more than 400 species on whale falls, at least 30 of them never seen anywhere else.","分布深度 ":"Depth range ","已有 ":""," 位探险者遇见过":" explorers have met it","你可能是第一个遇见它的探险者":"You may be the first explorer to meet it","小丑鱼":"Clownfish","偕老同穴（玻璃海绵）":"Venus’ flower basket (glass sponge)","深海贻贝、管栖蠕虫、细菌席":"Deep-sea mussels, tubeworms, bacterial mats","铁甲蜗牛":"Scaly-foot snail","深海偏顶蛤":"Deep-sea mussel","深水石珊瑚":"Deep-water stony coral","冰鱼":"Icefish","°（空气中 ":"° (","°）":"° in air)","（受海底影响）":" (affected by the seafloor)","≈0（波浪影响不到海底）":"≈0 (waves do not reach the seafloor)","波成沙纹 ":"Wave ripples ","流成沙纹 ":"Current ripples ","无":"None","自定义参数":"Custom settings"," · 当地时间 ":" · local time "," · 夜":" · night","<span class=\"sp unk\">还有 ":"<span class=\"sp unk\">"," 种未遇见</span>":" more not yet met</span>","<p><span class=\"tag\">含氧层</span>洞口一带是珊瑚礁，科考人员在龙洞上部记录到二十多种鱼。洞里的水和外面的海水几乎不交换，越往下越“老”。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Oxygenated layer</span>Around the mouth is a coral reef, and researchers have recorded more than twenty kinds of fish in the upper blue hole. The water inside barely exchanges with the sea outside, so the deeper you go, the “older” it is.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">化学跃层</span>氧气在这 30 m 里迅速耗尽，细菌开始改用硝酸盐、再用硫酸盐来“呼吸”。洞里约六成的氮在这一层被细菌转化成氮气流失。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Chemocline</span>Oxygen runs out within these 30 m, and bacteria switch to “breathing” nitrate and then sulfate. About 60% of the nitrogen in the hole is turned into nitrogen gas by bacteria in this layer and lost.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">无氧层</span>这里没有氧气，硫酸盐还原菌把硫酸盐变成硫化氢，硫化氢一直累积到约 150 m 后保持稳定。没有鱼、没有藻类，只有微生物；科研人员从龙洞里分离出的厌氧细菌中，约两成可能是新物种。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Anoxic layer</span>There is no oxygen here. Sulfate-reducing bacteria turn sulfate into hydrogen sulfide, which builds up to about 150 m and then stays steady. No fish, no algae, only microbes; about 20% of the anaerobic bacteria researchers isolated from the blue hole may be new species.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">浑浊层</span>氧化和还原的交界处是硫氧化细菌的乐园，它们在 100–140 m 占了微生物的约九成；再加上悬浮的有机颗粒，这一层的海水明显发浑，手电光被散射成一片雾。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Cloudy layer</span>The boundary between oxidising and reducing water is a paradise for sulfur-oxidising bacteria, which make up about 90% of the microbes at 100–140 m; with suspended organic particles as well, the water here is visibly cloudy, and a torch beam scatters into fog.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">传说</span>当地渔民称它为“南海之眼”。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Legend</span>Local fishermen call it the “Eye of the South China Sea”.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">透光层</span>阳光充足，大型动物在开阔的蓝水里巡游。往下看，海水一直蓝到看不见底。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Sunlight zone</span>Plenty of sunlight, and large animals cruise the open blue water. Looking down, the blue goes on further than you can see.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">暮光层</span>只剩微弱的蓝光。很多动物腹部长着发光器，把自己的影子“擦掉”，躲开下方的捕食者。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Twilight zone</span>Only a faint blue light is left. Many animals have light organs on their bellies that “erase” their shadow from predators below.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">午夜层</span>没有一丝阳光。这一层大约四分之三的动物都会发光。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Midnight zone</span>Not a trace of sunlight. About three quarters of the animals in this zone make light.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">深渊层</span>水温约 1.5 °C，食物主要靠上方飘落的海洋雪。生物稀少而缓慢。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Abyssal zone</span>Water about 1.5 °C; food comes mainly as marine snow drifting from above. Life is sparse and slow.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">超深渊</span>海沟里的世界。":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Hadal zone</span>The world of the trenches. ","狮子鱼在这里活动，它们是最深处的鱼。":"Snailfish live here, the deepest fish there are.","这里已经低于鱼类能生存的极限。":"This is already below the limit at which fish can survive.","<p><span class=\"tag\">迁移</span>二战时海军声呐在几百米深处发现一层会反射声波的“假海底”，白天在深处、夜里升到表层，后来才知道是成群的灯笼鱼、磷虾等动物。一些旧海图上至今还标着当年被误认成浅滩的地方。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Migration</span>In the Second World War, naval sonar found a sound-reflecting “false bottom” a few hundred metres down, deep by day and near the surface at night. Only later was it understood to be dense layers of lanternfish, krill and other animals. Some old charts still mark places once mistaken for shoals.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">海沟底部</span>卡梅隆描述这里是“完全没有起伏”的柔软平原，只看到小小的端足类。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Trench floor</span>Cameron described it as a soft plain “completely flat”, where he saw only small amphipods.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">海沟底部</span>细软的沉积物上住着巨型钩虾、海参和巨型单细胞生物。1960 年的的里雅斯特号和 2012 年卡梅隆都到过这里。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Trench floor</span>Giant amphipods, sea cucumbers and giant single-celled organisms live on the fine, soft sediment. The Trieste in 1960 and Cameron in 2012 both came here.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">珊瑚</span>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Corals</span>","。海底有 ":". The seafloor gets "," 的绿光供共生藻光合作用。</p>":" of the green light for the corals’ symbiotic algae.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">珊瑚</span>无造礁珊瑚：":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Corals</span>No reef-building corals: ","水温为 ":"the water is "," °C，低于约 18 °C":" °C, below about 18 °C","光照只剩 ":"light down to ","。</p>":".</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">巨藻</span>无：":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Kelp</span>None: ","水温高于约 20 °C，巨藻是冷水种":"water warmer than about 20 °C, and giant kelp is a cold-water species","光照不足":"not enough light","<p><span class=\"tag\">海扇</span>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Sea fans</span>","竹珊瑚被触碰时会沿枝条传出蓝色光波。":"Bamboo corals send a wave of blue light along their branches when touched.","扇面垂直于海流方向生长，最大化截留流过的浮游食物。":"The fan grows across the current to catch as much drifting plankton as possible.","<p><span class=\"tag\">栉水母</span>彩虹是纤毛衍射":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Comb jellies</span>The rainbow is made by cilia diffracting light","，这里没有光，打开手电才能看到。":"; there is no light here, so turn on a torch to see it.","入射光形成的，不是自己发光。":" that falls on them, not light of their own.","<p><span class=\"tag\">夜光</span>夜光藻被扰动时会闪蓝光，鱼群、海龟游过会留下光迹。":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Night glow</span>The dinoflagellate Noctiluca flashes blue when disturbed, so schools of fish and turtles leave trails of light. ","蓝光手电激发出珊瑚和海葵触手的绿色、橙红色荧光。":"The blue torch makes the tentacles of corals and anemones fluoresce green and orange-red.","试试蓝光手电看珊瑚荧光。":"Try the blue torch to see coral fluorescence.","<p><span class=\"tag\">深海</span>这里没有阳光。看到的光点都是生物发光：灯笼鱼的发光器、冠水母的报警光环、":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Deep sea</span>There is no sunlight here. Every point of light is bioluminescence: the photophores of lanternfish, the alarm ring of Atolla, ","鮟鱇的诱饵、":"the anglerfish’s lure, ","被扰动的浮游生物。</p>":"and disturbed plankton.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">热液</span>这里的生命不靠阳光：细菌把热液里硫化氢等物质的化学能转化成养分（化能合成），整个群落都建立在它们之上。龙旂已记录 21 类大型动物，其中 7 种是新种。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Vents</span>Life here does not depend on sunlight: bacteria turn the chemical energy of hydrogen sulfide and other substances in the vent fluid into food (chemosynthesis), and the whole community is built on them. 21 kinds of large animals have been recorded at Longqi, 7 of them new species.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">沉船鱼礁</span>1944 年 2 月的“冰雹行动”在这片泻湖里击沉了 45 艘以上的舰船。八十多年后，钢铁船体成了珊瑚、海绵和海鞘附着的基底：软珊瑚挂满高处的桅杆和吊杆，因为那里水流最好；甲板上结着成群的小鱼，船尾住着蓑鲉。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Wreck reef</span>Operation Hailstone in February 1944 sank more than 45 ships in this lagoon. More than eighty years later the steel hulls are a base for corals, sponges and sea squirts: soft corals cover the high masts and booms, where the current is best; schools of small fish gather above the deck, and lionfish live at the stern.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">蓝碳</span>海草床只占海底面积约 0.2%，却储存了海洋约 10% 的碳；它和红树林、盐沼一起被称为“蓝碳”生态系统。它们也是很多鱼虾的育幼场。</p><p><span class=\"tag\">儒艮</span>中国南方沿海曾有以海草为食的儒艮。2022 年发表的一项调查访问了 788 位渔民，自 2000 年以来没有任何可核实的目击记录，儒艮在中国已功能性灭绝，是中国水域第一种功能性灭绝的大型脊椎动物。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Blue carbon</span>Seagrass meadows cover only about 0.2% of the seafloor but store about 10% of the ocean’s carbon; with mangroves and salt marshes they are called “blue carbon” ecosystems. They are also nurseries for many fish and shrimp.</p><p><span class=\"tag\">Dugongs</span>Dugongs, which graze seagrass, once lived along China’s southern coast. A survey published in 2022 interviewed 788 fishers and found no verifiable sighting since 2000: the dugong is functionally extinct in China, the first large vertebrate to be functionally extinct in Chinese waters.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">深海平原</span>深海平原占地球表面一半以上，是地球上面积最大的生境。这里的食物几乎全靠上方几千米飘落的“海洋雪”，动物都长得慢、活得久。克拉里昂-克利珀顿区已记录到 5,578 种动物，约九成还没有被科学描述，而它也是全球最大的深海采矿勘探区。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Abyssal plain</span>Abyssal plains cover more than half of the Earth’s surface, the largest habitat on the planet. Food comes almost entirely as “marine snow” drifting down several kilometres, so animals grow slowly and live long. 5,578 animal species have been recorded in the Clarion-Clipperton Zone, about 90% of them not yet described by science, and it is also the world’s largest deep-sea mining exploration area.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">冷水珊瑚</span>这里没有阳光，珊瑚也没有共生藻，全靠洋流送来的浮游生物为生，所以冷水珊瑚礁总长在水流强的陆坡和海脊上。勒斯特礁全长三四十公里，是已知最大的冷水珊瑚礁，2002 年才被发现，同年周围约 300 km² 海域禁止底拖网。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Cold-water corals</span>There is no sunlight here and these corals have no symbiotic algae; they live entirely on plankton carried by the current, which is why cold-water reefs grow on slopes and ridges with strong currents. The Røst Reef is thirty to forty kilometres long, the largest cold-water coral reef known. It was discovered only in 2002, and in the same year bottom trawling was banned in about 300 km² around it.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">潮间带分带</span>同一块岩石上，越高的地方露出水面越久，要忍受日晒、干燥和温度剧变；越低的地方被淹得越久，但捕食者和竞争者更多。于是生物按高度排成一条条带子：滨螺、藤壶、龟足、贻贝、海藻依次往下。这种分带在世界各地的岩岸都能看到。</p><p><span class=\"tag\">潮汐</span>潮汐主要由月球引力引起，这里每天两涨两落，每次比前一天晚约 50 分钟。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Intertidal zones</span>On the same rock, higher spots are out of the water longer and must survive sun, drying and sharp temperature swings; lower spots are under water longer but face more predators and competitors. So life sorts itself into bands by height: periwinkles, barnacles, gooseneck barnacles, mussels and seaweeds, from top to bottom. You can see this zonation on rocky shores all over the world.</p><p><span class=\"tag\">Tides</span>Tides are caused mainly by the Moon’s gravity. Here there are two high and two low tides a day, each about 50 minutes later than the day before.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">海山</span>海山是从海底拔起、山顶仍在水下的山，大多是死火山，全球估计有几万座以上。它们把深层海流抬升、加速，带来更多食物，所以常长满珊瑚和海绵，聚集鱼群。</p><p><span class=\"tag\">温泉孵化</span>深海水温只有 1.6 °C，章鱼卵发育很慢；岩缝里的温泉最高 10.8 °C，章鱼妈妈平均约 1.8 年就能孵出小章鱼，大约相当于在 5 °C 的水里孵化。孵化越快，卵被吃掉、母亲饿死前失败的风险就越小。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Seamounts</span>Seamounts are mountains that rise from the seafloor with their summits still underwater; most are extinct volcanoes, and there are estimated to be tens of thousands of them. They lift and speed up deep currents, bringing more food, so they are often covered in corals and sponges and gather schools of fish.</p><p><span class=\"tag\">Warm-spring nursery</span>At 1.6 °C, octopus eggs develop very slowly in the deep sea. The warm springs in the cracks reach up to 10.8 °C, and mother octopuses hatch their young in about 1.8 years on average, roughly what it would take at 5 °C. The faster the eggs hatch, the less risk they are eaten or the mother starves before they do.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">冰缘</span>冰缘是北极春天最热闹的地方：冰底的冰藻先于浮游植物开始繁殖，端足类和桡足类啃食冰藻，北极鳕吃它们，一角鲸、白鲸、海豹和海鸟再吃北极鳕。北极鳕幼鱼体内 50–90% 的碳来自冰藻。</p><p><span class=\"tag\">海冰在减少</span>北极夏末的海冰面积 2012 年创下最低纪录；2025 年 9 月的最低值约 460 万平方公里，与 2008 年并列有卫星记录以来第 10 低。冰期变短，正改变一角鲸、白鲸和依赖海冰的整个食物网。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Floe edge</span>The floe edge is the busiest place in the Arctic spring: ice algae under the ice bloom before the phytoplankton, amphipods and copepods graze the algae, polar cod eat them, and narwhals, belugas, seals and seabirds eat the polar cod. 50–90% of the carbon in young polar cod comes from ice algae.</p><p><span class=\"tag\">Shrinking sea ice</span>Arctic sea ice at the end of summer hit a record low in 2012; the September 2025 minimum, about 4.6 million km², tied with 2008 as the 10th lowest since satellite records began. Shorter ice seasons are changing life for narwhals, belugas and the whole food web that depends on sea ice.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">冰下</span>头顶约 2 m 厚的海冰挡住了大部分阳光，只有冰洞里照下一道光柱。冬天之后的海水几乎没有浮游生物，清澈得能看到很远；水温 −1.9 °C，是海水的冰点。你呼出的气泡会贴在冰底聚成一片片“水银”。</p><p><span class=\"tag\">抗冻</span>这里的鱼血液里有抗冻糖蛋白，冰鱼甚至连血红蛋白都没有，血几乎是透明的。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Under the ice</span>About 2 m of sea ice overhead blocks most of the sunlight; only the dive hole lets a shaft of light through. After winter the water has almost no plankton and is clear enough to see a long way; it is −1.9 °C, the freezing point of seawater. Your exhaled bubbles stick to the underside of the ice in pools like “quicksilver”.</p><p><span class=\"tag\">Antifreeze</span>Fish here have antifreeze glycoproteins in their blood, and icefish do not even have haemoglobin, so their blood is almost clear.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">产卵</span>珊瑚不能移动，只好把繁殖押在“同时”上：整片礁在同一夜、同一小时释放配子，让卵和精子在水里相遇的机会最大，也让捕食者一时吃不完。1981 年科学家在大堡礁第一次记录到这种集体产卵，当时有 32 种珊瑚同时排放。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Spawning</span>Corals cannot move, so they bet their reproduction on timing: the whole reef releases its gametes on the same night, in the same hour, giving eggs and sperm the best chance to meet and giving predators more than they can eat. Scientists first recorded this mass spawning on the Great Barrier Reef in 1981, when 32 coral species spawned together.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">盐池</span>海底下方埋着古老的盐层，盐溶进渗出的流体，形成比海水重得多的卤水，在海底积成一个湖。湖里几乎没有氧气，误入的动物会死去；岸边却挤满了靠甲烷生活的贻贝。这个盐池 1989 年由美国海军的核动力研究潜艇 NR-1 首次探访，因此得名。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Brine pool</span>Ancient salt layers lie buried below the seafloor; salt dissolves into the seeping fluid, making brine far heavier than seawater, which pools into a lake on the seafloor. The lake has almost no oxygen, and animals that stray in die; yet its shore is crowded with mussels living on methane. The pool was first visited in 1989 by the US Navy’s nuclear-powered research submarine NR-1, which gave it its name.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">鲸落</span>据估计任何时候全球海底都躺着约 69 万具鲸骨，平均每隔约 12 km 就有一具；它们像深海里的绿洲，让生物得以在其间“跳岛”扩散。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Whale fall</span>At any moment an estimated 690,000 whale skeletons lie on the world’s seafloor, roughly one every 12 km; like oases in the deep, they let life “island-hop” between them.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">冷泉</span>海底渗出甲烷，细菌把它当能量来源，形成白色细菌席，养活贻贝床和管栖蠕虫。这里的气泡是甲烷，不是潜水员呼出的。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Cold seep</span>Methane seeps from the seafloor; bacteria use it for energy and form white bacterial mats, feeding mussel beds and tubeworms. The bubbles here are methane, not a diver’s breath.</p>","<p><span class=\"tag\">鱼群</span>沙丁鱼绕圈游成“鱼饵球”，翻身时银色鳞片会闪光。</p>":"<p><span class=\"tag\">Fish schools</span>Sardines circle into a “bait ball”, their silver scales flashing as they turn.</p>","暮光层 · 中层带":"Twilight zone · mesopelagic","午夜层 · 深层带":"Midnight zone · bathypelagic","深渊层":"Abyssal zone","超深渊层 · 海沟":"Hadal zone · trench","水温 ":"Water "," · 有氧":" · oxygenated"," · 氧气稀薄":" · little oxygen"," · 无氧 · 含硫化氢":" · anoxic · hydrogen sulfide","夜间":"Night","从关岛的礁壁出发，一路下潜到地球海洋最深处 10,935 m。沿途经过透光层、暮光层、午夜层、深渊层和海沟，各层的生物、水温、压强和光线都按实测资料变化。":"Set off from Guam’s reef wall and dive all the way to the deepest point of the world ocean, 10,935 m. On the way you pass through the sunlight, twilight, midnight, abyssal and hadal zones; the life, temperature, pressure and light of each zone change according to measured data.","左侧剖面里，珠穆朗玛峰按比例放进了海沟；可以在下方调倍速，或直接拖动深度条。":"In the profile on the left, Mount Everest is placed in the trench to scale. Change the speed below, or drag the depth bar.","按詹姆斯·卡梅隆 2012 年 3 月 26 日的真实时间线：05:15 出发，下潜 2 小时 36 分，在海底停留三个多小时，再上浮回到水面。":"Follows the real timeline of James Cameron’s dive on 26 March 2012: departure at 05:15, a 2 h 36 min descent, more than three hours on the bottom, then back up to the surface.","留意右下角的当地时间和字幕，它们对应当天的真实记录。":"Watch the local time and captions at the bottom right: they follow the real record of that day.","北太平洋开阔大洋 · 昼夜垂直迁移":"Open North Pacific · daily vertical migration","在一天 24 小时里看暮光层的动物黄昏上浮、黎明下沉。这是地球上规模最大的动物迁移，二战时的声呐曾把它误认成海底。":"Watch twilight-zone animals rise at dusk and sink at dawn over 24 hours. It is the largest animal migration on Earth; wartime sonar once mistook it for the seafloor.","点击下面的回声测深图跳到 19:00、50 m，看发光的迁移层从脚下升起。":"Click the echogram below to jump to 19:00 at 50 m and watch the glowing migrating layer rise from beneath you.","三沙永乐龙洞 · 蓝洞":"Yongle Blue Hole, Sansha · blue hole","西沙永乐环礁上的一口海底竖井，深约 301 m。沿洞壁从珊瑚礁一直下到洞底，穿过含氧层、化学跃层和充满硫化氢的无氧层。":"A seafloor shaft on Yongle Atoll in the Paracels, about 301 m deep. Follow the wall from the coral reef down to the bottom, through the oxygenated layer, the chemocline and the anoxic layer full of hydrogen sulfide.","100–150 m 的浑浊细菌层里能见度骤降；左侧剖面画的是洞的真实形状。":"Visibility drops sharply in the cloudy bacterial layer at 100–150 m; the profile on the left shows the real shape of the hole.","南海西沙群岛珊瑚礁 · 10 m":"Paracel Islands coral reef, South China Sea · 10 m","热带珊瑚礁：水清、光足，枝状和块状珊瑚长满礁石，海葵里住着小丑鱼，鹦嘴鱼和蝴蝶鱼在礁间觅食。":"A tropical coral reef: clear water, plenty of light, rocks covered in branching and massive corals, clownfish living in anemones, parrotfish and butterflyfish feeding among the coral.","切到“夜潜”，关掉手电，用手指或鼠标在水里快速划一划，看夜光藻闪光；打开蓝光手电则能看到珊瑚荧光。":"Switch to “Night dive”, turn off the torch and swipe a finger or the mouse quickly through the water to see Noctiluca flash; turn on the blue torch to see the corals fluoresce.","密克罗尼西亚特鲁克泻湖 · 富士川丸":"Truk Lagoon, Micronesia · Fujikawa Maru","一艘 133 m 长的二战日本飞机运输舰，1944 年在“冰雹行动”中被击沉，至今直立着坐在约 34 m 深的沙底上，后桅几乎伸出水面。":"A 133 m Japanese aircraft transport from the Second World War, sunk in Operation Hailstone in 1944. It still sits upright on sand about 34 m deep, its aft mast almost reaching the surface.","十几米深处红光已被海水吸收，软珊瑚看上去发暗；打开白光手电，它们才显出粉红、橙红的本色。从舱口往 2 号货舱里看，还能找到拆解的战斗机。":"Ten-odd metres down, the red light has been absorbed and the soft corals look dull; turn on the white torch and their true pinks and orange-reds appear. Look through the hatch into Hold No. 2 to find the dismantled fighters.","挪威罗弗敦外海 · 勒斯特冷水珊瑚礁 · 320 m":"Off Lofoten, Norway · Røst cold-water coral reef · 320 m","已知最大的冷水珊瑚礁，全长三四十公里。白色和橙色的深水石珊瑚长成一丛丛灌木，下面是层层堆积的死珊瑚骨架和碎屑；红色的泡泡糖珊瑚顺着海流张开，大眼的挪威平鲉悬停在礁上。":"The largest cold-water coral reef known, thirty to forty kilometres long. White and orange deep-water stony corals grow into bushes on top of layer upon layer of dead coral skeleton and rubble; red bubblegum corals open into the current, and big-eyed Norway redfish hover over the reef.","点击珊瑚看它每年只长几毫米；关掉手电，这片礁就完全沉入黑暗。":"Click a coral to see how it grows only a few millimetres a year; turn off the torch and the whole reef sinks into darkness.","加拿大北极 · 庞德因莱特浮冰边缘":"Canadian Arctic · Pond Inlet floe edge","北纬约 73°，巴芬岛北端的埃克利普斯海峡。冬天海面冻成约 1.8 m 厚、连着陆地不动的固定冰；春天它的外缘一点点碎裂后退，冰缘外是开阔水面。5 月底到 6 月，一角鲸和白鲸沿着冰缘向峡湾里迁移，冰底正是冰藻繁殖最旺的时候。":"About 73° N, in Eclipse Sound at the northern tip of Baffin Island. In winter the sea freezes into land-fast ice about 1.8 m thick; in spring its outer edge breaks up and retreats bit by bit, with open water beyond. From late May to June, narwhals and belugas migrate along the floe edge into the fjords, just when the ice algae under the ice are blooming most.","头顶是被冰藻染成褐色的冰底，挂着一缕缕北极直链藻；冰缘外明亮的开阔水里，一角鲸和白鲸的小群会沿着冰缘游过，不时上浮换气。点击冰底和冰缘看说明。":"Overhead is the underside of the ice, stained brown by ice algae and hung with strands of Melosira arctica; in the bright open water beyond the edge, small pods of narwhals and belugas swim along the floe edge and come up to breathe. Click the ice and the edge for explanations.","头顶是约 2 m 厚的海冰，阳光只透下百分之几，冰底被冰藻染成褐色，冰洞里照下一道光柱。水温 −1.9 °C，海底有红海星、南极海胆、玻璃海绵和巨型海蜘蛛，威德尔海豹不时从冰下游过。":"Overhead is about 2 m of sea ice that lets through only a few percent of the sunlight; its underside is stained brown by ice algae, and a shaft of light falls through the dive hole. The water is −1.9 °C; on the seafloor are red sea stars, Antarctic urchins, glass sponges and giant sea spiders, and Weddell seals pass under the ice now and then.","抬头看冰底的片状冰和贴在冰下的气泡；在海底找一找趴着不动、几乎透明的冰鱼。":"Look up at the platelet ice and the bubbles stuck under the ice; on the seafloor, look for icefish lying still, almost transparent.","海南陵水新村潟湖 · 海草床与红树林 · 1.6 m":"Xincun Lagoon, Lingshui, Hainan · seagrass and mangroves · 1.6 m","一个几乎被沙坝围住的潟湖。岸边是红树林，支柱根扎进软泥；往外是海菖蒲和泰来草组成的海草床。2007 年，新村港和相邻的黎安港一起设立了我国第一个以海草床为保护对象的特别保护区。":"A lagoon almost enclosed by a sandbar. Mangroves line the shore with prop roots in the soft mud; further out is a seagrass meadow of Enhalus and Thalassia. In 2007, Xincun and neighbouring Li’an lagoons became China’s first special protected area for seagrass beds.","左边是红树林的支柱根，小鱼在根间躲避捕食者；右边的海草随波摆动，水面上漂着海菖蒲的白色雄花。找找缠在海草上的海马和倒躺在泥上的倒立水母。":"On the left are the mangroves’ prop roots, where small fish hide from predators; on the right the seagrass sways with the waves, and white male Enhalus flowers float at the surface. Look for seahorses clinging to the seagrass and upside-down jellyfish lying on the mud.","温州平阳外海的南麂列岛，1990 年成为我国首批 5 个海洋自然保护区之一，1998 年加入联合国“人与生物圈”网络，以“贝藻王国”著称：已记录 422 种藻类、725 种贝类等软体动物。潮间带的岩石每天被海水淹没、露出各两次。":"The Nanji Islands, off Pingyang near Wenzhou, became one of China’s first five marine nature reserves in 1990 and joined UNESCO’s Man and the Biosphere network in 1998. Known as the “kingdom of shellfish and algae”, they have 422 recorded species of algae and 725 of shellfish and other molluscs. The intertidal rocks are covered and uncovered by the sea twice a day.","让潮汐播放起来，看海面怎样一点点淹过藤壶带和贻贝床；藤壶一被淹没就伸出蔓足捕食。也可以拖动“潮位”停在任一时刻。":"Let the tide play and watch the sea creep over the barnacle zone and the mussel beds; as soon as barnacles are covered, they stretch out their legs to feed. You can also drag “Tide level” to stop at any moment.","加州戴维森海山 · 章鱼花园 · 3,200 m":"Davidson Seamount, California · octopus garden · 3,200 m","蒙特雷西南约 129 km 的一座死火山，长 42 km、从海底拔起约 2,280 m。山脚一座小丘上，岩缝里渗出地热加温的海水，几千只珍珠章鱼聚在这里产卵、孵卵——2018 年才被发现，是已知最大的深海章鱼聚集地。":"An extinct volcano about 129 km south-west of Monterey, 42 km long and rising about 2,280 m from the seafloor. On a small hill at its foot, geothermally warmed water seeps from cracks in the rock, and thousands of pearl octopuses gather here to lay and brood their eggs. Discovered only in 2018, it is the largest known gathering of deep-sea octopuses.","看温泉上方水的“抖动”，那是温水折射光线；章鱼妈妈的外套膜在一张一缩地给卵泵水。点击岩石和温泉看说明。":"Watch the water “shimmer” above the springs: warm water bending the light. The mother octopuses’ mantles swell and relax as they pump water over their eggs. Click the rocks and the springs for explanations.","太平洋克拉里昂-克利珀顿区 · 深海平原 · 4,100 m":"Clarion-Clipperton Zone, Pacific · abyssal plain · 4,100 m","夏威夷与墨西哥之间一片约 600 万平方公里的深海平原，水深 4,000–6,000 m，水温约 1.5 °C。海底铺满土豆大小的锰结核，每一百万年只长 1–10 cm。这里已记录到 5,578 种动物，约九成从未被科学描述。":"An abyssal plain of about 6 million km² between Hawaii and Mexico, 4,000–6,000 m deep, with water at about 1.5 °C. The seafloor is strewn with potato-sized manganese nodules that grow only 1–10 cm in a million years. 5,578 animal species have been recorded here, about 90% never described by science.","在手电光里找沿着自己的取食痕迹爬行的长尾蝶参、成群的海猪、用鳍条“站”在海底的三脚架鱼。右边那条没有结核的宽带是 1979 年采矿试验留下的车辙，点击它看 44 年后的样子。":"In the torchlight, look for sea cucumbers crawling along their own feeding trails, herds of sea pigs, and tripod fish “standing” on the seafloor on their fin rays. The wide band without nodules on the right is the track left by a 1979 mining test; click it to see it 44 years later.","海南三亚鹿回头 · 珊瑚产卵之夜":"Luhuitou, Sanya, Hainan · coral spawning night","春季满月前后的某几个夜里，鹿角珊瑚在 21 点后的约一小时内集体释放红色的卵精束。它们缓缓上浮，像一场倒着下的雪。":"On a few nights around the spring full moon, Acropora corals release red egg–sperm bundles together within about an hour after 9 pm. They drift slowly upwards like snow falling the wrong way.","把时间拖到 21:00 之前，可以看到珊瑚表面布满“含着”的卵精束；21:30 之后抬头看水面聚起的浮层。":"Drag the time before 21:00 to see corals dotted with bundles “held” ready; after 21:30, look up at the slick gathering at the surface.","加州蒙特雷湾巨藻林 · 12 m":"Kelp forest, Monterey Bay, California · 12 m","冷水上升流养出的海底森林。巨藻随涌浪整片摆动，水温约 12 °C，对造礁珊瑚来说太冷了。":"An underwater forest fed by cold upwelling. Giant kelp sways as a whole with the swell; the water, about 12 °C, is too cold for reef-building corals.","在“环境参数”里调大有效波高或波周期，看巨藻和海底沙纹怎样变化。":"Under “Environment”, raise the wave height or period and watch the kelp and the sand ripples change.","红海埃拉特中光层礁 · 55 m":"Mesophotic reef, Eilat, Red Sea · 55 m","红海的海水极清，55 m 深处仍有几个百分点的阳光。光越弱，珊瑚越长成扁平的盘状，好接住更多光。":"The Red Sea is extremely clear, and a few percent of the sunlight still reaches 55 m. The weaker the light, the flatter the corals grow, into plates that catch more of it.","看面板里的“此处剩余阳光”：红光几乎为零，所以这里的一切都是蓝绿色。":"Look at “Sunlight left here” in the panel: red is almost zero, so everything here is blue-green.","南海北部陆坡 · 600 m":"Northern South China Sea slope · 600 m","暮光层的底部，阳光几乎耗尽，只有手电照亮的一小片海底。竹珊瑚在陆坡的硬底上长成一片“珊瑚园”，被触碰时会沿枝条传出蓝光；灯笼鱼、银斧鱼在这一带活动。":"The bottom of the twilight zone. The sunlight is almost gone; only the patch of seafloor in your torchlight is lit. Bamboo corals grow in a “coral garden” on the hard ground of the slope and send blue light along their branches when touched; lanternfish and hatchetfish live here.","关掉手电，剩下的光点全部来自生物发光。":"Turn off the torch: every point of light left is bioluminescence.","南海海马冷泉 · 1,390 m":"Haima cold seep, South China Sea · 1,390 m","海底渗出甲烷，细菌把它当作能量来源，养活了贻贝床、管栖蠕虫和白色的细菌席。这里冒出的气泡是甲烷。":"Methane seeps from the seafloor, and bacteria use it as an energy source, feeding mussel beds, tubeworms and white bacterial mats. The bubbles rising here are methane.","点击贻贝、管栖蠕虫和细菌席，看它们怎样靠化学能生活。":"Click the mussels, tubeworms and bacterial mats to see how they live on chemical energy.","墨西哥湾 NR1 海底盐池 · 650 m":"NR1 brine pool, Gulf of Mexico · 650 m","比海水重得多的卤水在海底积成一个湖，有清晰的湖面和湖岸。湖里没有氧气，岸边却挤满了靠甲烷生活的贻贝。":"Brine far heavier than seawater has pooled into a lake on the seafloor, with a clear surface and shoreline. The lake has no oxygen, yet its shore is crowded with mussels living on methane.","点击湖面会荡开慢慢的波纹；贴近湖面斜看，湖面才会像镜子一样倒映出对岸。":"Click the lake surface to send out slow ripples; look along the surface at a low angle and it mirrors the far shore.","蒙特雷峡谷鲸落 · 1,800 m":"Whale fall, Monterey Canyon · 1,800 m","一头灰鲸沉到海底后，几十年里会依次养活食腐动物、食骨蠕虫和靠硫化物生活的细菌群落。":"After a grey whale sinks to the seafloor, it feeds scavengers, bone-eating worms and then sulfide-based bacterial communities in turn for decades.","拖动面板里“经过的时间”滑块，从几周快进到几十年。":"Drag the “Time elapsed” slider in the panel to fast-forward from weeks to decades.","西南印度洋龙旂热液区 · 2,800 m":"Longqi vent field, Southwest Indian Ocean · 2,800 m","300 多摄氏度的热液从黑烟囱喷出。周围的盲虾、铁甲蜗牛、雪人蟹完全不靠阳光，而是靠细菌把热液里的化学能转化成养分。":"Vent fluid above 300 °C gushes from black smokers. The blind shrimp, scaly-foot snails and yeti crabs around them do not rely on sunlight at all, but on bacteria that turn the chemical energy of the vent fluid into food.","点击烟囱和动物，看它们分别住在离热源多远的地方。":"Click the chimneys and the animals to see how far from the heat each one lives.","在“环境参数”里改深度、水温、水质、海流和波浪，场景会按同样的物理和生态规则重新生成。":"Change the depth, temperature, water type, current and waves under “Environment”, and the scene is rebuilt by the same physical and ecological rules.","<b>看点</b>":"<b>Look for</b> ","把深度拖到 200 m 以下，看珊瑚和阳光怎样消失。":"Drag the depth below 200 m and watch the corals and the sunlight disappear.","珊瑚只在夜里产卵":"Corals spawn only at night","这一场景固定在夜里；想看白天的珊瑚礁，请选“西沙 · 珊瑚礁”。":"This scene is set at night; for the coral reef by day, choose “Paracels · coral reef”.","展开":"Show","锰结核（多金属结核）":"Manganese nodules (polymetallic nodules)","直径约 4–12 cm · 每百万年只长 1–10 cm":"About 4–12 cm across · grow only 1–10 cm per million years","以鲨鱼牙齿、贝壳碎片等为核心，从海水和沉积物孔隙水里一层层析出锰、铁的氧化物，并富集镍、钴、铜。克拉里昂-克利珀顿区平均每平方米约有 15 kg。在一片软泥里，结核是难得的硬底，海绵、珊瑚、海葵等很多固着动物只能长在它们上面。":"Layer by layer around a core such as a shark tooth or shell fragment, manganese and iron oxides precipitate from seawater and from the water in the sediment, enriched in nickel, cobalt and copper. The Clarion-Clipperton Zone averages about 15 kg of nodules per square metre. In a plain of soft mud the nodules are rare hard ground, and many attached animals such as sponges, corals and anemones can grow only on them.","克拉里昂-克利珀顿区 · 约 4,100 m":"Clarion-Clipperton Zone · about 4,100 m","1979 年采矿试验的车辙":"Track from a 1979 mining test","宽约 8 m · 44 年后几乎没有变化":"About 8 m wide · almost unchanged after 44 years","1979 年，一台约 100 吨重的集矿机在这一海区做了太平洋最早的工业深海采矿试验：清走一条约 8 m 宽的结核，压出两道深沟。2023 年科学家重访，车辙看起来和刚压出时差不多；巨型单细胞生物和小型活动动物已部分回来，但很多动物数量仍然偏少，固着在海底的大型动物几乎没有恢复（Jones 等，Nature，2025）。画面中的车辙按论文描述示意。":"In 1979 a collector weighing about 100 tonnes ran the Pacific’s first industrial deep-sea mining test here, clearing a strip of nodules about 8 m wide and pressing two deep furrows. When scientists returned in 2023 the track looked much as it had when it was made; giant single-celled organisms and small mobile animals had partly come back, but many animals were still fewer, and the large animals attached to the seafloor had barely recovered (Jones et al., Nature, 2025). The track in the scene is drawn from the paper’s description.","深海软泥":"Deep-sea ooze","沉积物积累得极慢 · 水温约 1.5 °C":"Sediment builds up extremely slowly · water about 1.5 °C","深海平原铺着细软的软泥，主要是从上方几千米慢慢飘落的“海洋雪”和微小的浮游生物骨骼。海参等动物一边爬一边吞食它，身后留下取食痕迹；那些小黑点是穴居动物的洞口。":"The abyssal plain is covered in fine, soft ooze, mostly “marine snow” that drifted slowly down several kilometres and the tiny skeletons of plankton. Sea cucumbers and other animals swallow it as they crawl, leaving feeding trails behind; the small dark dots are burrow entrances.","长尾蝶参":"Long-tailed sea cucumber","深海平原 · 深渊层":"Abyssal plain · abyssal zone","海猪":"Sea pig","三脚架鱼（深海狗母鱼）":"Tripod fish","约 900–4,700 m":"About 900–4,700 m","深海长尾鳕":"Abyssal grenadier (rattail)","约 2,000–4,700 m":"About 2,000–4,700 m","深海蛇尾":"Deep-sea brittle star","深海平原":"Abyssal plain","有柄玻璃海绵":"Stalked glass sponge","Hyalonema 等":"Hyalonema and others","深海平原 · 长在结核上":"Abyssal plain · grows on nodules","身体半透明，背后竖着一面高高的“尾帆”，外号“橡皮软糖松鼠”。它一边在海底爬一边吞食沉积物，身后留下长长的取食痕迹：海底那些弯弯曲曲的浅色带子就是这样来的。":"Translucent, with a tall “sail” raised at its back, nicknamed the “gummy squirrel”. It swallows sediment as it crawls along the seafloor, leaving long feeding trails behind: the pale winding bands on the seafloor are made this way.","用几对鼓胀的管足在海底“行走”，常常成群出现，面朝水流吃沉积物里的有机碎屑。":"It “walks” on the seafloor on a few pairs of swollen tube feet, often in herds, facing into the current to eat organic scraps in the sediment.","用两根腹鳍鳍条和一根尾鳍鳍条把身体撑离海底，面朝水流一动不动，等着漂来的小动物。它雌雄同体，找不到配偶时可以自体受精。":"It props itself above the seafloor on two pelvic fin rays and one tail ray, facing into the current without moving, waiting for small animals to drift by. It is a hermaphrodite and can fertilise itself if it cannot find a mate.","深海里最常见的鱼之一：大头、细长的“鼠尾”，常头朝下贴着海底慢慢游，靠嗅觉寻找落到海底的动物尸体。":"One of the commonest fish in the deep sea: a big head and a long thin “rat tail”. It often swims slowly head-down near the seafloor, smelling out dead animals that have fallen there.","深海平原上数量最多的大型动物之一，靠五条细长的腕划动着移动。":"One of the most numerous large animals on the abyssal plain, it moves by rowing with five long thin arms.","用一束长长的玻璃质骨针固定在锰结核上。2016 年科学家在夏威夷外海 4,000 多米处发现一种幽灵般的白色章鱼，把卵产在死去海绵的柄上，而这些海绵只能长在结核这样的硬底上。":"It is anchored to manganese nodules by a long bundle of glassy spicules. In 2016 scientists found a ghostly white octopus more than 4,000 m deep off Hawaii laying its eggs on the stalks of dead sponges, and these sponges can grow only on hard ground such as nodules.","三脚架鱼":"Tripod fish","海菖蒲的雄花":"Male Enhalus flowers","直径约几毫米 · 漂在水面上":"A few millimetres across · floating on the surface","海菖蒲是开花植物。雄花成熟后脱离植株浮上水面，像一粒粒白色小泡沫随水漂动；雌花长在长柄上伸到水面，两者在水面相遇完成授粉。":"Enhalus is a flowering plant. When ripe, the male flowers break off and float to the surface, drifting like tiny white bubbles; the female flowers reach the surface on long stalks, and the two meet there for pollination.","新村潟湖":"Xincun Lagoon","潟湖软泥":"Lagoon mud","细颗粒淤泥 · 富含有机质":"Fine silt · rich in organic matter","红树林和海草的叶片落下、腐烂，连同潮水带来的细泥一起沉积下来，把大量碳埋进泥里，几百上千年都不会释放。那些小洞是蟹和蠕虫的洞穴，白色碎屑是贝壳。":"Mangrove and seagrass leaves fall and rot, settling with fine silt brought by the tides and burying large amounts of carbon in the mud, where it stays locked away for hundreds or thousands of years. The small holes are crab and worm burrows; the white bits are shell fragments.","海菖蒲":"Enhalus (tape seagrass)","潮间带至约 4 m":"Intertidal to about 4 m","泰来草":"Thalassia (turtle grass)","潮间带至浅海":"Intertidal to shallow sea","红海榄":"Rhizophora (red mangrove)","红树林 · 潮间带":"Mangroves · intertidal","白骨壤":"Avicennia (grey mangrove)","牡蛎":"Oyster","潮间带 · 红树林根上":"Intertidal · on mangrove roots","大海马":"Spotted seahorse","海草床 · 浅海":"Seagrass meadows · shallow sea","仙后水母（倒立水母）":"Cassiopea (upside-down jellyfish)","红树林与海草床浅水":"Shallow water among mangroves and seagrass","世界上最大的海草之一，带状叶片长 30–150 cm，靠粗壮的地下茎扎在软泥里抵御风浪和潮流。":"One of the largest seagrasses in the world, with strap-like leaves 30–150 cm long, anchored in soft mud by thick underground stems against waves and tides.","叶片较短而弯，常和海菖蒲混生。海草不是海藻，而是从陆地回到海里的开花植物，有根、茎、叶，靠地下茎在泥里蔓延。":"Its leaves are shorter and curved, often mixed with Enhalus. Seagrasses are not seaweeds but flowering plants that returned to the sea from land, with roots, stems and leaves, spreading through the mud by underground stems.","一根根弯曲的支柱根把树干撑在潮间带的软泥上，也挡住了风浪。根间是小鱼小虾躲避捕食者的“育儿所”。":"Curved prop roots hold the trunk up on the soft intertidal mud and break the waves. The spaces between the roots are a “nursery” where small fish and shrimp hide from predators.","从泥里竖起一根根铅笔似的呼吸根，在缺氧的淤泥里给根系通气。":"Pencil-like breathing roots stand up out of the mud, bringing air to the roots in the oxygen-poor silt.","附着在被潮水淹没的根和石头上，靠过滤海水里的浮游生物为生，同时帮助净化水质。":"Attached to roots and stones covered by the tide, it lives by filtering plankton from the water and helps clean it.","用尾巴缠住海草，靠伪装和吸管一样的嘴吸食小型甲壳动物。海马由雄性的育儿袋孵育后代。":"It wraps its tail around seagrass and sucks up small crustaceans with its straw-like mouth, relying on camouflage. In seahorses the male carries the young in his brood pouch.","倒着躺在泥上、口腕朝上，因为体内共生的藻类要晒太阳进行光合作用；被惊扰时会放出带刺细胞的黏液。":"It lies upside down on the mud with its oral arms facing up, because the symbiotic algae in its body need sunlight to photosynthesise; when disturbed it releases mucus full of stinging cells.","倒立水母":"Upside-down jellyfish","北极海冰的底面":"Underside of the Arctic sea ice","约 1.8 m 厚的岸冰 · 冰底 −1.8 °C":"Land-fast ice about 1.8 m thick · −1.8 °C at its underside","冬天冻结、贴着海岸不动的“固定冰”。春天积雪变薄、日照变长，冰底的冰藻大量繁殖，把冰染成褐色。冰下的光只有水面的百分之几，冰藻能在只有水面约 0.02% 的光下进行光合作用。雪薄的地方更亮。":"“Fast ice” freezes in winter and stays attached to the coast. In spring, as the snow thins and the days lengthen, ice algae on its underside bloom and stain it brown. The light under the ice is only a few percent of that at the surface, yet ice algae can photosynthesise with as little as about 0.02%. It is brighter where the snow is thin.","埃克利普斯海峡 · 庞德因莱特":"Eclipse Sound · Pond Inlet","浮冰边缘（冰缘）":"Floe edge","固定冰与开阔水面的交界":"Where the fast ice meets open water","这一侧是连着陆地、整片不动的固定冰，另一侧是开阔水面。冰缘随季节向陆地后退。春天，冰藻、浮游植物、北极鳕和鲸都聚集在这条线上，因纽特人世代在这里狩猎。冰块底下发褐的一层就是冰藻。":"On this side is unbroken fast ice attached to the land; on the other, open water. The floe edge retreats towards land with the season. In spring, ice algae, phytoplankton, polar cod and whales all gather along this line, and the Inuit have hunted here for generations. The brownish layer on the underside of the ice blocks is ice algae.","一角鲸":"Narwhal","北极 · 浮冰边缘和峡湾":"Arctic · floe edges and fjords","白鲸":"Beluga","北极与亚北极":"Arctic and subarctic","北极鳕":"Polar cod","北冰洋 · 冰下":"Arctic Ocean · under the ice","冰下端足类":"Ice amphipod","北冰洋 · 海冰底面":"Arctic Ocean · underside of the sea ice","北极直链藻":"Melosira arctica","雄性的长牙是左上颌的一颗牙齿，螺旋生长，可达 2 m 以上，表面有多达一千万个神经末梢。成年雄性体长约 4.5 m。它们能潜到 1,500 m 以下，一次超过 25 分钟。全球约四分之三的一角鲸在加拿大海域。":"The male’s tusk is an upper-left tooth that grows in a spiral to more than 2 m, with up to 10 million nerve endings on its surface. Adult males are about 4.5 m long. They can dive below 1,500 m for more than 25 minutes at a time. About three quarters of the world’s narwhals live in Canadian waters.","成年白鲸全身雪白，体长可达约 4.9 m；幼崽是深灰色的，随年龄慢慢变白。颈椎没有愈合，能点头、左右转头，便于在浮冰间穿行；额头圆圆的“额隆”柔软，帮助聚焦和调整发出的声音。叫声丰富，被称为“海中金丝雀”。":"Adult belugas are pure white and grow to about 4.9 m; calves are dark grey and turn white slowly with age. Their neck vertebrae are not fused, so they can nod and turn their heads, which helps them move among the ice floes; the soft, rounded “melon” on the forehead helps focus and shape the sounds they make. They are so vocal they are called “sea canaries”.","北极食物网的枢纽：吃冰下的端足类和桡足类，又是一角鲸、白鲸、海豹和海鸟的主要食物。幼鱼躲在海冰的缝隙里，身体里 50–90% 的碳最终来自冰藻。":"The hub of the Arctic food web: it eats amphipods and copepods under the ice and is the main food of narwhals, belugas, seals and seabirds. Young polar cod hide in cracks in the sea ice, and 50–90% of the carbon in their bodies ultimately comes from ice algae.","一辈子贴着海冰底面生活，啃食冰藻。北极鳕的幼鱼主要吃它们，冰藻的能量就这样一级级传上去。海冰减少，它们的家也在缩小。":"It spends its whole life on the underside of the sea ice, grazing ice algae. Young polar cod feed mainly on them, passing the energy of the ice algae up the food chain step by step. As the sea ice shrinks, so does their home.","一种硅藻，细胞连成长链，在冰底挂成一缕缕金褐色的“帘子”，可长到 1 m 以上。冰融化时成团快速沉到几千米深的海底，给那里的生物送去食物。2012 年海冰最少的夏天，它贡献了北冰洋中部约 45% 的初级生产。":"A diatom whose cells link into long chains, hanging from the ice in golden-brown “curtains” that can grow longer than 1 m. When the ice melts it sinks rapidly in clumps to the seafloor thousands of metres down, delivering food there. In 2012, the summer with the least sea ice, it made up about 45% of the primary production in the central Arctic Ocean.","戴维森海山的枕状熔岩":"Pillow lava of Davidson Seamount","已熄灭的海底火山 · 约 900 万–1,500 万年前形成":"Extinct submarine volcano · formed about 9–15 million years ago","海底火山喷出的熔岩一遇冷水，外壳立刻凝固，里面的岩浆再把它撑破、挤出，堆成一个个“枕头”。戴维森海山长 42 km、宽 13 km，从海底拔起约 2,280 m，山顶仍在水下 1,250 m。山上记录到 237 种生物、27 类深海珊瑚，2009 年起归入蒙特雷湾国家海洋保护区。":"When lava from an undersea volcano meets cold water its skin freezes at once; the molten rock inside then bursts through and squeezes out again, piling up into “pillows”. Davidson Seamount is 42 km long and 13 km wide and rises about 2,280 m from the seafloor, its summit still 1,250 m underwater. 237 species and 27 kinds of deep-sea coral have been recorded on it, and since 2009 it has been part of Monterey Bay National Marine Sanctuary.","戴维森海山 · 约 3,200 m":"Davidson Seamount · about 3,200 m","温泉":"Warm spring","裂缝里的水最高约 10.8 °C · 周围只有 1.6 °C":"Water in the cracks up to about 10.8 °C · only 1.6 °C around it","海山脚下的岩石裂缝里渗出被地热加温的海水。水几乎看不出颜色，唯一的迹象是水面上方像海市蜃楼一样的“抖动”——那是温水和冷水密度不同，让光线发生折射。":"Geothermally warmed water seeps from cracks in the rock at the foot of the seamount. It has almost no colour; the only sign is a mirage-like “shimmer” above it, light bent by the different densities of warm and cold water.","戴维森海山 · 章鱼花园":"Davidson Seamount · octopus garden","珍珠章鱼（孵卵中）":"Pearl octopus (brooding)","约 3,200 m · 戴维森海山":"About 3,200 m · Davidson Seamount","章鱼花园":"Octopus garden","捕食性螺":"Predatory snail","Buccinoidea 等":"Buccinoidea and others","深海小虾":"Deep-sea shrimp","雌章鱼把卵产在温泉渗出的岩缝上，然后倒伏在卵上一动不动地守护，不吃东西，直到卵孵化后死去。2018 年发现这里时，一小块 2.5 公顷的范围内就数出 5,718 只，其中 4,707 只在孵卵，整片可能超过两万只。温水让卵约 1.8 年就孵化，在冰冷的深海里要长得多。":"The female lays her eggs on the rock where the warm spring seeps out, then lies over them without moving to guard them, eating nothing, until they hatch and she dies. When the site was found in 2018, 5,718 octopuses were counted in just 2.5 hectares, 4,707 of them brooding, and the whole garden may hold more than twenty thousand. The warm water lets the eggs hatch in about 1.8 years; in the icy deep sea it would take much longer.","夹在孵卵的章鱼妈妈之间，吃刚孵出的小章鱼和死去的母亲，把能量留在这片“花园”里。":"Tucked between the brooding mothers, it eats newly hatched octopuses and mothers that have died, keeping the energy in this “garden”.","在章鱼窝之间爬行，吃被遗弃的卵、捕捉刚孵出的小章鱼。":"It crawls between the octopus nests, eating abandoned eggs and catching hatchlings.","小虾在章鱼窝周围游走，捡食没有母亲守护的卵。":"Small shrimp roam around the nests, picking off eggs no mother is guarding.","珍珠章鱼":"Pearl octopus","高潮":"high tide","低潮":"low tide","涨潮":"rising","落潮":"falling","滨螺带":"periwinkle zone","藤壶带":"barnacle zone","龟足":"gooseneck barnacles","贻贝床":"mussel beds","鼠尾藻":"Sargassum thunbergii","珊瑚藻与马尾藻":"coralline algae and Sargassum","距上一次低潮 ":""," 小时。现在淹在水下：":" hours since low tide. Under water now: ","、":", ","只有潮下带的海藻和海胆":"only the seaweeds and urchins below the tide line","。藤壶被淹没时会伸出蔓足捕食，露出水面就关紧壳板保水。":". Barnacles stretch out their legs to feed when covered by the sea, and close their plates tight to keep water in when exposed.","▶ 播放潮汐":"▶ Play tide","南麂列岛的岩礁海岸":"Rocky shore of the Nanji Islands","“贝藻王国” · 浙江温州平阳":"“Kingdom of shellfish and algae” · Pingyang, Wenzhou, Zhejiang","潮水每天涨落两次，岩石上同一个高度被淹没的时间是固定的，于是生物按高度排成一条条带子：最高处是黑色的蓝藻带和滨螺，往下是白花花的藤壶带，再往下是黑紫色的贻贝床，最低处是粉红的珊瑚藻和成片的马尾藻。南麂列岛已记录 422 种藻类、725 种贝类等软体动物，1998 年成为我国第一个加入联合国“人与生物圈”的海洋保护区。":"The tide rises and falls twice a day, so each height on the rock is covered for a fixed share of the time, and life sorts itself into bands by height: at the top a black band of cyanobacteria and periwinkles, below it the white barnacle zone, then dark purple mussel beds, and at the bottom pink coralline algae and stands of Sargassum. 422 species of algae and 725 of shellfish and other molluscs have been recorded in the Nanji Islands, which in 1998 became China’s first marine reserve in UNESCO’s Man and the Biosphere network.","南麂列岛国家级海洋自然保护区":"Nanji Islands National Marine Nature Reserve","鳞笠藤壶":"Tetraclita barnacle","潮间带中高潮区":"Mid to high intertidal","潮间带岩缝":"Intertidal crevices","厚壳贻贝":"Thick-shelled mussel","潮间带中低潮区":"Mid to low intertidal","短滨螺":"Periwinkle (Littorina brevicula)","潮间带高潮区":"High intertidal","鼠尾藻与马尾藻":"Sargassum","潮间带至潮下带":"Intertidal to subtidal","绿海葵":"Green anemone","潮间带低潮区":"Low intertidal","紫海胆":"Purple sea urchin","低潮线以下岩礁":"Rocky reef below the low-tide line","藤壶是甲壳动物，幼体漂流一阵后头朝下粘在岩石上，一辈子不再移动。涨潮时打开壳板、伸出羽毛似的蔓足扫食浮游生物；退潮时关紧壳板，把一点海水锁在里面熬过几个小时的日晒。":"Barnacles are crustaceans. The larvae drift for a while, then glue themselves head-down to rock and never move again. At high tide they open their plates and sweep the water for plankton with feathery legs; at low tide they shut tight, locking in a little seawater to last through hours of sun.","也是一种藤壶，有一根肉质的柄，顶端一簇尖尖的壳板像乌龟的脚，因此叫“龟足”。成群挤在浪大的岩缝里。":"Also a barnacle, but with a fleshy stalk topped by a cluster of pointed plates like a turtle’s foot. They crowd together in wave-beaten crevices.","用足丝把自己牢牢粘在岩石上，层层叠叠铺成贻贝床，经得住大浪。它们滤食浮游生物，床缝里又住着许多小动物。":"It glues itself firmly to rock with byssal threads, building up layered mussel beds that can withstand big waves. Mussels filter plankton, and many small animals live in the gaps of the bed.","住在潮间带最高处，退潮时能在空气里待很久，靠刮食岩石上的微藻和蓝藻为生。":"It lives at the very top of the intertidal and can stay in air for a long time at low tide, scraping microalgae and cyanobacteria off the rock.","鼠尾藻矮小粗壮，长在潮间带较高处；更低处的马尾藻能长得很高，靠小小的气囊让藻体在水里立起来。南麂列岛的潮下带上部几乎全被马尾藻覆盖。":"Sargassum thunbergii is short and stout and grows higher on the shore; lower down, other Sargassum species grow tall, held upright in the water by tiny air bladders. The upper subtidal of the Nanji Islands is almost entirely covered by Sargassum.","退潮时缩成一团、身上粘着碎壳和沙粒防晒，涨潮后才张开触手。":"At low tide it pulls into a ball, covered in bits of shell and sand against the sun, and opens its tentacles only when the tide comes in.","躲在低潮线以下的岩缝里啃食海藻，是我国东南沿海常见的食用海胆。":"It hides in crevices below the low-tide line grazing seaweed; it is a common edible sea urchin on China’s south-east coast.","马尾藻":"Sargassum","已切换到流畅模式":"Switched to smooth mode","画面较卡，已自动降低分辨率和重复生物的数量。可以在控制台“时间与照明”下面改回高画质。":"The view was stuttering, so the resolution and the number of repeated animals and plants have been reduced. You can switch back to high quality under “Time and lighting” in the console.","头顶":"overhead","正下方":"straight below","正前方":"straight ahead","左前方":"ahead left","右前方":"ahead right","左边":"to your left","右边":"to your right","身后":"behind you","偏上":", above","偏下":", below","，约 ":", about ","夜里，没有阳光":"night, no sunlight","阳光充足":"plenty of sunlight","阳光变暗，颜色偏蓝绿":"the sunlight is fading and colours turn blue-green","只剩微弱的蓝光":"only a faint blue glow is left","没有阳光，一片漆黑":"no sunlight, completely dark","手电关着":"torch off","开着蓝光手电":"blue torch on","开着白光手电":"white torch on","你在哪里":"Where you are","环境":"Conditions","水深 ":"Depth ","压强 ":"Pressure ","光线：":"Light: ","；":"; ","大约能看清 ":"You can see about "," m 以内":" m","几乎什么都看不见，只有会发光的生物":"You can see almost nothing except animals that make their own light","附近看得见的生物":"Animals you can see nearby","附近暂时没有看到动物。试试打开手电、换个地点，或者等一会儿。":"No animals in view right now. Try switching on the torch, changing place, or waiting a little.","可以试试":"Things to try","，水深 ":", depth ","，附近看得见 ":", "," 种生物。":" kinds of animals within sight.","推进器加速度约 0.9 m/s²，最高速度约 1 m/s；海流和波浪会推着你漂。缆绳长 60 m。":"Thruster acceleration about 0.9 m/s², top speed about 1 m/s; currents and waves push you around. The tether is 60 m long.","北":"N","东北":"NE","东":"E","东南":"SE","南":"S","西南":"SW","西":"W","西北":"NW","速度 ":"Speed "," m/s · 航向 ":" m/s · heading "," · 离底 ":" · above bottom "," m · 缆绳 ":" m · tether "," · 缆绳已放到头":" · tether fully out"," · 水流 ":" · current ","珊瑚礁新手":"Reef rookie","在热带珊瑚礁认识 5 种生物。":"Get to know 5 species on a tropical coral reef.","珊瑚礁只占海底面积的不到 1%，却养活了约四分之一的海洋物种。":"Coral reefs cover less than 1% of the seafloor yet support about a quarter of all marine species.","会发光的深海":"The glowing deep","找到 3 种会发光的生物（深海、夜里或冰下都有）。":"Find 3 animals that make light (in the deep, at night or under the ice).","在深海的水层里，约四分之三的动物会发光，大多发出海水最透明的蓝光。":"In the open water of the deep sea about three quarters of animals make light, mostly the blue that seawater transmits best.","不靠阳光的生命":"Life without sunlight","找到 3 种靠化学能（甲烷或硫化物）生活的生物。":"Find 3 organisms that live on chemical energy (methane or sulfide).","1977 年在加拉帕戈斯热液区的发现，让人们第一次知道整个生态系统可以不依赖阳光。":"The discovery at the Galápagos vents in 1977 showed for the first time that a whole ecosystem can exist without sunlight.","遇见巨兽":"Meet the giants","在下潜途中遇见鲸鲨、抹香鲸和大王乌贼。":"Meet a whale shark, a sperm whale and a giant squid on the way down.","抹香鲸能下潜到两千米以下捕食大王乌贼，两者的搏斗至今没有人亲眼见过。":"Sperm whales dive below two kilometres to hunt giant squid; no one has ever seen the two fight.","到达最深处":"Reach the deepest point","下潜到挑战者深渊，10,900 m 以下。":"Dive to the Challenger Deep, below 10,900 m.","至今只有二十多人到过挑战者深渊；首次是 1960 年的的里雅斯特号。":"Only about two dozen people have ever been to the Challenger Deep; the first was the Trieste in 1960.","鲸落的三幕":"Three acts of a whale fall","在鲸落找齐盲鳗、睡鲨和食骨蠕虫（拖动时间滑块）。":"Find hagfish, a sleeper shark and bone-eating worms at the whale fall (drag the time slider).","一头鲸的遗体能在深海养活一个群落几十年。":"One whale carcass can feed a deep-sea community for decades.","夜里的迁移":"Migration by night","在昼夜垂直迁移场景里，夜里在 100 m 以浅遇见灯笼鱼。":"In the daily vertical migration scene, meet lanternfish shallower than 100 m at night.","中层鱼类的总重量可能超过一百亿吨，它们每晚上下迁移，把表层的碳带进深海。":"Mesopelagic fish may weigh more than ten billion tonnes in total; migrating up and down every night, they carry carbon from the surface into the deep.","极端之地":"Extreme places","到过热液喷口、海底盐池、蓝洞的无氧层和南极海冰之下。":"Visit a hydrothermal vent, a brine pool, the anoxic layer of the blue hole and the water under the Antarctic sea ice.","这些地方的高温、高盐、无氧或冰冷，让科学家思考：地外海洋里会不会也有生命。":"The heat, salt, lack of oxygen or cold of these places make scientists wonder whether life could exist in oceans beyond Earth.","冰下的生命":"Life under the ice","在南极海冰下遇见冰鱼和威德尔海豹。":"Meet an icefish and a Weddell seal under the Antarctic sea ice.","冰鱼的血里没有血红蛋白，是唯一这样的脊椎动物。":"Icefish have no haemoglobin in their blood, the only vertebrates like this.","冰缘的独角兽":"Unicorns of the floe edge","在北极浮冰边缘遇见一角鲸和白鲸。":"Meet a narwhal and a beluga at the Arctic floe edge.","一角鲸的长牙其实是一颗牙齿，表面有多达一千万个神经末梢。":"The narwhal’s tusk is actually a tooth, with up to 10 million nerve endings on its surface.","一年一度的夜":"One night a year","看到鹿角珊瑚集体产卵。":"See staghorn corals spawn together.","珊瑚集体产卵直到 1981 年才被科学家第一次完整记录。":"Scientists first fully recorded mass coral spawning only in 1981.","自由驾驶员":"Free pilot","用自由驾驶累计游出 50 m。":"Travel a total of 50 m in free piloting.","系缆式水下机器人（ROV）是今天深海科考的主力工具之一。":"Tethered underwater robots (ROVs) are among the main tools of deep-sea research today.","图鉴达人":"Field guide expert","图鉴收集 50 种生物。":"Collect 50 species in the field guide.","科学家估计海洋里约九成的物种还没有被描述过。":"Scientists estimate that about 90% of species in the ocean have not yet been described.","\">前往</button>":"\">Go</button>","已完成 ":"Completed ","这里太亮了":"Too bright here","生物发光很微弱，白天在浅水里看不到。切到“夜潜”，或者到 200 m 以下，再用手指或鼠标在水里划一划。":"Bioluminescence is faint and cannot be seen in shallow water by day. Switch to “Night dive” or go below 200 m, then swipe a finger or the mouse through the water.","声速 m/s":"Sound speed m/s","声道轴 约 ":"Channel axis ≈ ","声源深度 ":"Source depth "," m · 25 条声线中有 ":" m · "," 条被困在声道里（不碰海面也不碰海底），可以一直传下去；灰色的声线撞到海面或海底，每撞一次都会损失能量。":" of 25 rays are trapped in the channel (touching neither the surface nor the bottom) and can travel on and on; the grey rays hit the surface or the bottom and lose energy every time they do.","这个浏览器不支持网页音频。":"This browser does not support web audio.","这个声源深度下，没有声线能不碰海面和海底地传到 1,000 km 外。把声源移到声道轴附近再试。":"At this source depth, no ray reaches 1,000 km without touching the surface or the bottom. Move the source near the channel axis and try again.","1,000 km 外的接收器先听到斜着走的声线（它们穿过更快的水层，先到），最后才是沿声道轴走的声线，所以声音越来越密、在最后戛然而止，这正是 1944 年 Ewing 和 Worzel 第一次听到的“SOFAR 信号”。到达时间跨度约 ":"A receiver 1,000 km away first hears the steep rays (they pass through faster water and arrive first), and last of all the rays travelling along the channel axis, so the sound grows denser and then stops abruptly: exactly the “SOFAR signal” Ewing and Worzel first heard in 1944. Arrivals span about ","（这里压缩到 6 秒播放）":" (compressed here to 6 seconds of playback)","约 ":"About "," m · 深海声道轴":" m · deep sound channel axis","这里的声速最慢（约 ":"Sound is slowest here (about "," m/s）。上面的水暖、下面的水压高，声音都会被“折”回这一层，低频声音能沿着它传几千公里，鲸的叫声也能借它远距离传播。":" m/s). Warm water above and high pressure below both bend sound back into this layer, so low-frequency sound can travel thousands of kilometres along it, and whale calls can use it to carry far.","\" fill=\"#e9e4d8\" stroke=\"#bfb8a8\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">泡沫杯</text>":"\" fill=\"#e9e4d8\" stroke=\"#bfb8a8\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">Foam cup</text>","\" fill=\"#ff7a63\" opacity=\".85\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">装空气的气球</text>":"\" fill=\"#ff7a63\" opacity=\".85\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">Air-filled balloon</text>","\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#5ea8ff\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">装满水的瓶子</text>":"\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#5ea8ff\" opacity=\".8\"/><text x=\"500\" y=\"222\" text-anchor=\"middle\" class=\"pt\">Bottle full of water</text>"," 个大气压</b>，相当于每平方厘米上压着 <b>":" atmospheres</b>, the same as <b>"," 吨":" tonnes","</b>。<br>气球体积：原来的 <b>":"</b> pressing on every square centimetre.<br>Balloon volume: <b>","%</b>（回到水面会恢复）；泡沫杯：原来的 <b>":"%</b> of the original (it recovers at the surface); foam cup: <b>","%</b>，高度约原来的 <b>":"%</b> of the original, height about <b>","%</b>（回到水面也不会恢复）；水：原来的 <b>":"%</b> (it will not recover at the surface); water: <b>","%</b>。":"%</b> of the original.","在地图上点两个点，就能画出这两点之间的海底剖面":"Click two points on the map to draw the seafloor profile between them","剖面长约 ":"The profile is about "," km，最深处水深约 ":" km long; its deepest point is about "," m，":" m deep, ","最浅处水深约 ":"its shallowest point is about ","最高处海拔约 ":"its highest point is at an elevation of about ","。图里的竖直方向被放大了约 ":". The vertical scale is exaggerated about "," 倍；按真实比例画，几千米的起伏放在几百上千公里宽的剖面上，几乎就是一条平线。":" times; at true scale, relief of a few kilometres across a profile hundreds or thousands of kilometres wide would be almost a flat line.","正在加载全球地形数据（约 0.8 MB）…":"Loading global relief data (about 0.8 MB)…","地形数据加载失败，请检查网络后关闭再打开。":"The relief data failed to load. Check your connection, then close and reopen.","（点击前往）":" (click to go)","水深约 ":"Depth about ","海拔约 ":"Elevation about ","按真实地点与实测数据模拟":"Simulated from real places and measured data","拍不了明信片":"Can’t take a postcard","这个浏览器不允许读取三维画面。":"This browser does not allow reading the 3D view.","点“保存图片”会把这张明信片下载到你的设备；手机上也可以长按图片保存。":"“Save image” downloads this postcard to your device; on a phone you can also press and hold the image to save it.","点“保存图片”会弹出确认框，确认后图片会保存到你的设备。":"“Save image” opens a confirmation box; once you confirm, the image is saved to your device.","这里不能直接保存文件：电脑上右键图片“另存为”，手机上长按图片保存。":"Files can’t be saved directly here: on a computer right-click the image and choose “Save as”; on a phone press and hold the image.","海底明信片-":"seafloor-postcard-","已交给浏览器下载。":"Handed to the browser to download.","已交给浏览器保存。":"Handed to the browser to save.","已取消保存。":"Save cancelled.","已有一个保存确认框，请先处理它。":"A save confirmation box is already open; please deal with it first.","这里暂时不能保存：电脑上右键图片“另存为”，手机上长按图片保存。":"Saving isn’t available here right now: on a computer right-click the image and choose “Save as”; on a phone press and hold the image.","· 共 ":"· "," 位探险者":" explorers in all","· 还没有人留下记录":"· No records yet","你遇见过的生物里，「":"Of the animals you have met, “","」目前只有你一个人见过。":"” has so far been seen only by you.","你遇见过的生物里，最少人见过的是「":"Of the animals you have met, the one seen by the fewest explorers is “","」：共 ":"”: "," 人遇见过。":" explorers have met it.","你可以看到大家的数字，但你的发现只保存在这台设备上、没有计入共享图鉴：分享这个页面的人给你的权限是“查看者”。想被计入，请对方在“分享”里把你设为“参与者（Contributor）”。":"You can see everyone’s numbers, but your finds are saved only on this device and are not counted in the shared field guide: the person who shared this page gave you “viewer” access. To be counted, ask them to make you a “Contributor” under Share.","登录 Claude 后打开，你的发现才会计入共享图鉴；现在只保存在这台设备上。":"Sign in to Claude and open the page to have your finds counted in the shared field guide; for now they are saved only on this device.","共享图鉴的存储已满，你的新发现暂时没能计入。":"The shared field guide’s storage is full, so your new finds could not be counted for now.","你的 ":"Your "," 种发现已计入共享图鉴（只记录遇见了哪些生物，不记录名字或位置）。":" finds are counted in the shared field guide (only which animals were met is recorded, not names or locations).","遇见第一种生物后，你的发现会自动计入共享图鉴（只记录遇见了哪些生物，不记录名字或位置）。":"After you meet your first animal, your finds are counted in the shared field guide automatically (only which animals were met is recorded, not names or locations).","<b>手机分屏 VR</b>：把手机横过来；有纸盒眼镜就放进去，没有也可以直接看。<br>转动手机（或用手指拖动）看四周，<b>轻点屏幕</b>开始或停止朝视线方向游动。":"<b>Phone split-screen VR</b>: turn the phone sideways; put it in a cardboard viewer if you have one, or just look directly.<br>Turn the phone (or drag with a finger) to look around, and <b>tap the screen</b> to start or stop swimming where you look.","这个页面读不到手机的陀螺仪（浏览器不支持，或者没有允许访问“动作与方向”），画面不会跟着手机转。<b>用手指左右上下拖动</b>来看四周，轻点屏幕开始或停止游动。":"This page can’t read the phone’s gyroscope (the browser doesn’t support it, or access to “Motion & Orientation” wasn’t allowed), so the view won’t follow the phone. <b>Drag with a finger</b> to look around, and tap the screen to start or stop swimming."," · 游动中":" · swimming","已退出头显 VR。":"Left headset VR.","没能进入头显 VR：":"Couldn’t enter headset VR: ","浏览器拒绝了请求":"the browser refused the request","。可以改用上面的手机分屏 VR。":". You can use the phone split-screen VR above instead.","这台设备的浏览器没有提供头显 VR（WebXR），所以这里只有手机分屏模式。用 VR 头显时，请在头显自带的浏览器里打开这个页面。":"This device’s browser does not offer headset VR (WebXR), so only split-screen mode is available here. With a VR headset, open this page in the headset’s own browser.","检测到 VR 头显，可以用“进入头显 VR”。头显模式里没有泛光和白平衡后期处理，颜色会比屏幕上偏蓝一些。":"VR headset detected: you can use “Enter headset VR”. Headset mode has no bloom or white-balance post-processing, so colours look a little bluer than on screen.","海洋覆盖地球 71% 的表面":"The ocean covers 71% of the Earth’s surface","导览从南海西沙 10 m 深的珊瑚礁出发。珊瑚礁只占海底面积不到 1%，却养活了约四分之一的海洋物种。":"The tour starts on a coral reef 10 m deep in the Paracel Islands. Coral reefs cover less than 1% of the seafloor yet support about a quarter of all marine species.","海草床与红树林":"Seagrass and mangroves","海南陵水新村潟湖。红树林的支柱根是小鱼的育幼场，海草随波摆动。海草床只占海底约 0.2%，却储存了海洋约 10% 的碳。":"Xincun Lagoon, Lingshui, Hainan. Mangrove prop roots are a nursery for small fish, and the seagrass sways with the waves. Seagrass meadows cover only about 0.2% of the seafloor but store about 10% of the ocean’s carbon.","南麂列岛：潮间带":"Nanji Islands: the intertidal","潮水每天两涨两落。岩石上的生物按高度排成带：滨螺、藤壶、龟足、贻贝和海藻。藤壶被淹没时会伸出蔓足捕食。":"The tide rises and falls twice a day. Life on the rock sorts into bands by height: periwinkles, barnacles, gooseneck barnacles, mussels and seaweeds. Barnacles stretch out their legs to feed when the sea covers them.","巨藻林：海底的森林":"Kelp forest: a forest under the sea","加州蒙特雷湾的冷水上升流带来养分，巨藻长成十几米高的森林，随涌浪整片摆动。":"Cold upwelling in Monterey Bay, California, brings nutrients, and giant kelp grows into forests more than ten metres tall that sway together with the swell.","沉船变成的鱼礁":"A shipwreck turned reef","富士川丸 1944 年沉没，八十年后船身已被软珊瑚和鱼群占据。十几米深处，红光已被海水吸收，一切都偏蓝绿。":"The Fujikawa Maru sank in 1944; eighty years later its hull is taken over by soft corals and fish. Ten-odd metres down, red light has been absorbed by the water and everything looks blue-green.","南极海冰之下":"Under the Antarctic sea ice","水温 −1.9 °C，海水因为含盐而不结冰。头顶两米厚的海冰只透下百分之几的阳光，冰底的冰藻是南大洋食物链的起点。":"The water is −1.9 °C, and seawater stays liquid because it is salty. Two metres of ice overhead let through only a few percent of the sunlight, and ice algae on its underside start the Southern Ocean food chain.","北极浮冰边缘":"The Arctic floe edge","固定冰在这里断开，外面是开阔水面。冰底被冰藻染成褐色，挂着直链藻；一角鲸和白鲸沿着冰缘游过，上浮换气。":"The fast ice breaks off here, with open water beyond. Its underside is stained brown by ice algae and hung with Melosira; narwhals and belugas swim along the edge and come up to breathe.","一年中只有满月前后的几个夜里，珊瑚同时释放红色的卵精束，缓缓上浮，像一场倒着下的雪。":"On only a few nights around the full moon each year, corals release red egg–sperm bundles together, drifting slowly upwards like snow falling the wrong way.","320 m：没有阳光的珊瑚礁":"320 m: a coral reef without sunlight","挪威外海的冷水珊瑚不靠阳光，靠捕食海流带来的浮游生物。勒斯特礁全长三四十公里，是已知最大的冷水珊瑚礁。":"The cold-water corals off Norway don’t rely on sunlight; they catch plankton brought by the current. The Røst Reef is thirty to forty kilometres long, the largest cold-water coral reef known.","1,390 m：靠甲烷生活":"1,390 m: living on methane","南海海马冷泉从海底渗出甲烷，细菌把它变成养分，养活了贻贝床、管栖蠕虫和白色的细菌席。":"At the Haima cold seep in the South China Sea, methane seeps from the seafloor and bacteria turn it into food, feeding mussel beds, tubeworms and white bacterial mats.","650 m：海底的湖":"650 m: a lake on the seafloor","比海水重得多的卤水在海底积成湖，有湖面也有湖岸。湖里没有氧气，岸边却挤满了靠甲烷生活的贻贝。":"Brine far heavier than seawater has pooled into a lake on the seafloor, with a surface and a shore. There is no oxygen in the lake, yet its shore is crowded with mussels living on methane.","1,800 m：鲸落":"1,800 m: a whale fall","一头鲸沉到深海，能养活一个群落几十年。科学家已在鲸落上记录到 400 多种生物。":"A whale that sinks to the deep sea can feed a community for decades. Scientists have recorded more than 400 species on whale falls.","2,800 m：热液喷口":"2,800 m: hydrothermal vents","300 多摄氏度的热液从黑烟囱喷出。周围的盲虾和雪人蟹完全不靠阳光，靠细菌把化学能变成养分。":"Vent fluid above 300 °C gushes from black smokers. The blind shrimp and yeti crabs around them don’t rely on sunlight at all; bacteria turn chemical energy into food.","3,200 m：海山章鱼花园":"3,200 m: the seamount octopus garden","戴维森海山脚下的岩缝渗出温泉，几千只珍珠章鱼聚在这里孵卵。温水上方的“抖动”是光线在冷热水交界处折射。":"Warm springs seep from cracks at the foot of Davidson Seamount, and thousands of pearl octopuses gather here to brood their eggs. The “shimmer” above the warm water is light bending where warm and cold water meet.","4,100 m：深海平原":"4,100 m: the abyssal plain","海底铺满土豆大小的锰结核，一百万年只长 1–10 cm。这片海区已记录到五千多种动物，约九成从未被科学描述；那条没有结核的宽带，是 1979 年采矿试验留下的车辙。":"The seafloor is strewn with potato-sized manganese nodules that grow only 1–10 cm in a million years. More than five thousand animal species have been recorded in this region, about 90% never described by science; the wide band without nodules is the track left by a 1979 mining test.","最后一站：马里亚纳海沟":"Last stop: the Mariana Trench","从关岛礁壁出发，一路下潜到地球海洋最深处。光、水温和生物会随深度一层层改变；左侧剖面显示你的位置。":"From Guam’s reef wall, dive all the way to the deepest point of the world ocean. Light, temperature and life change layer by layer with depth; the profile on the left shows where you are.","结束":"End","语音讲解：加载失败":"Narration: failed to load","语音讲解：":"Narration: ","MiniMax 语音合成的讲解配音":"Narration voiced by MiniMax speech synthesis","导览结束":"End of the tour","已退出展览模式":"Left exhibition mode","现在可以自由探索：拖动画面看四周，点击生物看它是谁，控制台里还有蓝洞、昼夜迁移等场景。":"Now you can explore freely: drag to look around, click animals to see what they are, and find more scenes such as the blue hole and the daily migration in the console.","10,935 m：地球海洋最深处":"10,935 m: the deepest point of the world ocean","这里的压力超过 1,000 个大气压，水温只有 2 °C 多。即使到了今天，人类对深海的了解仍然非常有限。":"The pressure here is over 1,000 atmospheres and the water just over 2 °C. Even today, we still know very little about the deep sea.","你从 10 m 的珊瑚礁一路走到了 10,935 m 的海沟底。现在可以自由探索：控制台里还有蓝洞、昼夜垂直迁移等场景，也可以开着水下机器人四处看看。":"You have travelled from a 10 m coral reef to the floor of the trench at 10,935 m. Now you can explore freely: the console has more scenes such as the blue hole and the daily vertical migration, or you can take an underwater robot out for a look."};
